  - TypeFullName: BasisContentVersion
    MemberName: BasisContentVersion
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Content-version policy for cached bees: decides whether an on-disc
      cache entry may still be\n used for a requested version, and normalizes the
      opaque tags that decision runs on.\n\n \n\nCache identity is the remote url,
      so re-uploading a bee to the SAME url used to be\n invisible to every client
      that already had it cached \u2014 the load path never touched the network\n
      again. A version tag rides alongside the url so \"same address, new bytes\"
      becomes expressible.\n\n\n\nAn empty requested tag means \"no opinion\", and
      the cache is then authoritative. Every\n bundle published before versioning,
      every client built before it, and the GUID-per-upload flow\n all produce empty
      tags, so they keep the exact pre-existing behavior."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: BasisContentVersion
    MemberName: VersionRefreshThrottleSeconds
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 1
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Minimum spacing between version-triggered re-downloads of the same
      url.\n\n \n\nA tag that arrives over the network is attacker-controlled: a
      peer that broadcasts a\n different tag every few seconds would otherwise make
      every client in the instance re-download\n that avatar on command \u2014 bandwidth
      amplification aimed at the publisher's own host. The\n throttle bounds a hostile
      peer to one refresh per url per window while leaving a genuine\n update (which
      settles after a single refresh, because the observed validator then matches)\n
      completely unaffected.\n\n\n\nUser-driven refreshes do not pass through here
      \u2014 they evict the entry outright."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: BasisContentVersion
    MemberName: LastModifiedPrefix
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 1
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Marks a stored tag as having come from `Last-Modified` rather than
      an `ETag`, so it\n can be turned back into the right conditional request header.
      Tags are stored VERBATIM\n otherwise (quotes and weak markers intact) because
      `If-None-Match` must echo the\n server's exact spelling; normalization happens
      only when comparing."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
