  - TypeFullName: 
    MemberName: CanonicalizeRemoteUrl
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(url)
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Canonical form of a remote bee URL for cache-identity purposes (disc-meta
      keys and\n in-memory bundle keys). The same location arrives in different spellings
      \u2014 avatar\n records carry escaped paths (\"Dooly%20Sailor3\") while other
      sources carry raw ones\n (\"Dooly Sailor3\"), with host casing differing too.
      Raw string equality treats those\n as different bees, so each flow redownloads
      and overwrites the other's cache meta\n every session. Absolute http(s) URLs
      normalize scheme/host casing and path escaping;\n anything else (local paths,
      empty) returns trimmed input."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
