  - TypeFullName: Basis.EventDriver.IBasisFrameSync
    MemberName: IBasisFrameSync
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "One per-frame main-thread callback, polled by BasisEventDriver from
      the\n single window in LateUpdate where every avatar transform is main-thread
      safe.\n\n That window sits between the network transmit (`AfterAvatarChanges`,
      which reads the\n local bones inline) and `JigglePhysics.DispatchSimulate`,
      which is where the jiggle\n transform jobs are scheduled. By the time it runs,
      IK and the local player sim have posed\n the avatar, authored motion has written,
      the constraint solve is fenced, and the remote\n bone jobs are joined \u2014
      and nothing has been dispatched yet. Reading or writing a Transform\n here
      therefore cannot race a TransformAccessArray job or stall the main thread on
      one, and\n a write lands early enough that JigglePhysics samples it this frame
      rather than next.\n\n Implementations must be main-thread only and must not
      assume they are the only entry:\n order between entries is registration order
      and is not a contract."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
