  - TypeFullName: BasisCalibrationMirror
    MemberName: BasisCalibrationMirror
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The calibration panel's personal see-through mirror: shows ONLY the
      local avatar, floating on a\n transparent background, without closing the menu
      when it opens.\n\n Spawns the same embedded \"Personal Mirror\" addressable
      the Library pin uses, but skips\n ContentLoader.LoadProp because every placement
      branch there calls BasisMainMenu.Close() \u2014 this\n mirror must live beside
      the open calibration panel. The reflection cameras are culled to the\n LocalPlayerAvatar
      layer only (a large perf win in busy instances) and cleared to (0,0,0,0); the\n
      surface is swapped to the transparent BasisMirrorCutout shader, which routes
      the sampled\n reflection's alpha into the material's Alpha, so only the opaque
      avatar reads as solid.\n Registered into BasisCalibrationMirrorService so the
      calibration panel (framework\n assembly, which cannot reference this one) can
      drive it."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
