  - TypeFullName: BasisCalibrationMirrorRelay
    MemberName: BasisCalibrationMirrorRelay
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: MonoBehaviour
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Makes the calibration visuals visible inside the calibration cutout
      mirror.\n\n The cutout mirror culls its reflection cameras to the LocalPlayerAvatar
      layer, so anything on\n Default never appears in it. Two calibration visual
      systems live on Default:\n 1. Tracker visuals \u2014 the \"calibration balls\"
      (FallbackSphere / real device models) BasisInput\n    spawns per tracked device,
      shown by VisibleTrackers during calibration. These are what\n    players line
      their pucks up with.\n 2. BasisGizmoManager visuals \u2014 the lock-in proximity
      spheres and tracker link lines are\n    batched draws submitted on BasisGizmoManager.RenderLayer,
      and text labels are objects\n    under the runtime \"Parent Of Debug Data\"
      container.\n\n Widening the reflection mask to Default would drag the entire
      opaque world into the see-through\n cutout; instead this relayers ONLY those
      objects onto LocalPlayerAvatar (and points the gizmo\n RenderLayer at it).
      The main camera renders that layer anyway (it's how you see your own body),\n
      so nothing disappears from the world view. Lives on the mirror instance and
      restores every\n touched object's original layer on teardown."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
