  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Avatar.BasisCalibrationLockInVisualizer
    MemberName: BasisCalibrationLockInVisualizer
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Calibration \"lock-in\" aid. While the player holds the T-pose waiting
      to pull the triggers, each\n full-body avatar bone draws a proximity sphere
      AT THE BONE plus a line connecting it to the\n nearest tracker, so you can
      read how well each tracker latches onto the bone it will drive. The\n sphere
      shrinks and both it and the connecting line go amber -> green as the tracker
      closes on the\n bone; for feet the color also folds in foot-forward alignment
      so a positionally-close but\n mis-rotated foot will not green.\n\n It anchors
      to the live avatar bones (BasisLocalBoneControl.OutgoingWorldData), NOT a synthetic\n
      HMD-relative frame, so the guides sit on the avatar instead of floating in
      front of it. Unlike the\n debug calibration spheres in BasisLocalBoneDriver
      it is NOT gated by the ShowGizmos master toggle:\n it owns its own AfterSimulateOnRender
      subscription, live only between Begin and\n End. All proximity/alignment math
      lives in BasisCalibrationLockInCore.\n\n Foot-rotation note: the alignment
      color uses the TRACKER's forward, which matches the foot's\n forward only for
      conventionally-mounted pucks \u2014 it is an aim aid (feet forward and flat),
      not an\n absolute foot-direction readout."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
