  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Avatar.BasisLocalAvatarNetworkNotice
    MemberName: BasisLocalAvatarNetworkNotice
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Warns the local player when the avatar they are wearing is a file only
      this machine has.\n\n \n\nAn avatar is broadcast as a bare URL that every remote
      then resolves for itself. A\n `file://` URL names nothing outside this machine,
      so each remote's load throws and\n latches `HasFailedAvatarLoadGlobally` \u2014
      they are left on the loading dummy for the rest\n of the session and never
      retry. None of that comes back over the wire, so the machine that\n chose the
      avatar is the only place it can be explained.\n\n\n\nBuilt-in avatars load
      by Addressable key out of each client's own build instead of by\n URL, so they
      carry across fine even though they are equally \"not hosted anywhere\" \u2014
      both\n ends already ship the asset. That is why only BasisLoadMode.Download
      is\n considered here."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
