  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.BasisHighPlayerCapPerformanceMode
    MemberName: BasisHighPlayerCapPerformanceMode
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Watches the instance population and, once per app run for each population
      tier, offers to\n switch BasisPerformanceMode on at the level that tier warrants.
      Pumped from\n the central tick; no MonoBehaviour.\n\n Each tier asks at most
      once per app lifetime \u2014 the static \"asked\" flags reset on restart,\n
      so the offer comes back the next time the app is launched into a crowded instance.
      Crossing\n a higher tier supersedes the lower ones (their flags are marked
      asked at the same time), so\n joining an already-huge instance shows a single
      prompt instead of stacking several.\n\n The dialogue lists the values the level
      will actually resolve to, read back from the mode\n itself, so the text can
      never drift from the effect. Nothing here is asked when the player\n has already
      turned the mode on to at least that level, or has it following the population\n
      automatically."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
