  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.BasisPanelInputDelay
    MemberName: BasisPanelInputDelay
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: MonoBehaviour
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Swallows presses that land on a panel in the first moments after it
      opens. A panel\n that appears under the pointer would otherwise take the second
      half of an accidental\n double press as a real click on whatever it happens
      to have put there.\n \n\n\n The dead time is scoped to the panel that just
      opened, so everything already on\n screen keeps responding immediately and
      rapid clicking elsewhere is unaffected. The\n press is not queued: the pointer
      has to be released and pressed again deliberately."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
