  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.BasisPerformanceMode
    MemberName: BasisPerformanceMode
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Reversible, multi-level Performance Mode.\n\n \n\nThe mode owns a table
      of graphics / crowd / avatar-cost settings. Turning it\n on snapshots the player's
      own values, then writes the level's preset over the top;\n turning it off writes
      the snapshot back. Nothing is lost, so the mode can be flipped\n from the hotbar
      or the Graphics tab at any time, including mid-instance.\n\n\n\nA preset value
      is never applied verbatim: it is combined with the snapshot so\n the result
      is the cheaper of the two. A player who already runs tighter limits than\n
      the preset keeps their own, and no level can ever make anything more expensive
      than\n it was before the mode was switched on.\n\n\n\nEdits the player makes
      to a controlled setting while the mode is on are folded\n back into the snapshot,
      so they survive turning the mode off again."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
