  - TypeFullName: BasisCameraTargetMsaa
    MemberName: BasisCameraTargetMsaa
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "URP only honours a camera target texture's own MSAA level while the
      pipeline asset itself has\n MSAA enabled (`camera.allowMSAA && asset.msaaSampleCount
      > 1` in InitializeCameraData), so\n with the Antialiasing setting Off the camera
      target descriptor reports one sample while the\n texture is really multisampled.
      An offscreen camera with no post-processing then gets no\n intermediate colour
      attachment \u2014 the multisampled sample count was the only thing asking for
      one\n \u2014 and URP renders straight into the multisampled surface without
      ever running the explicit\n resolve the Editor and desktop players require,
      leaving the surface shaders sample blank.\n Size every camera target texture
      through Clamp."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
