  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Constraints.BasisConstraintSystem
    MemberName: BasisConstraintSystem
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Batched solver behind the BasisConstraintBase components. Every enabled\n
      constraint in the process \u2014 avatar or scene \u2014 is flattened into one
      set of native containers\n and solved by three jobs per frame (sample, solve,
      write), instead of each component paying\n for its own `Update` and its own
      scattered transform reads.\n\n Components announce themselves through the SDK-side
      static events rather than calling in\n directly, because the SDK assembly cannot
      reference this one. The subscription is installed\n once at RuntimeInitializeLoadType.SubsystemRegistration,
      before any scene\n loads, so no component can enable ahead of the listener.\n\n
      Structural changes (a component joining, leaving, or reshaping its source list)
      set\n `sDirty` and rebuild the whole table on the next Schedule. That is a\n
      deliberate simplification over the incremental append `BasisAuthoredMotionSystem`
      does:\n constraint counts are small and structural churn is rare, whereas the
      shared source buffer\n makes incremental compaction fiddly to get right. Scalar
      edits \u2014 weight, offsets, masks,\n rest pose, source weights \u2014 are
      re-read every frame and never trigger a rebuild, so\n animating a constraint's
      weight stays free.\n\n Reparenting a constrained transform at runtime does
      not invalidate anything on its own;\n call BasisConstraintBase.SetDirty after
      doing so, since the cached parent row\n is resolved at rebuild."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
