  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Device_Management.
    MemberName: CanEnterMode
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 2
    ParamNames:
    - mode
    - blockedReason
    ParamDocs:
    - The mode being offered or requested.
    - Localized explanation when the result is `false`; otherwise null.
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Whether `mode` can be entered right now.\n \n\n\n Once one XR plug-in
      has initialized it owns the graphics device for the rest of the\n process,
      so the other VR runtime cannot take over without a restart \u2014 attempting
      it\n only tears the working runtime down and lands in Desktop. The mode is
      refused here\n instead, and the platform panel greys its entry out with `blockedReason`\n
      as the hover tooltip so the greyed control explains itself.\n \n\n\n The live
      runtime is read from the XR loader rather than the current mode, so a soft\n
      swap to Desktop (which deliberately keeps the runtime alive) still blocks the
      switch."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
