  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Device_Management.BasisProtonDetection
    MemberName: BasisProtonDetection
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Detects whether this Windows build is actually running on top of a
      Windows\n compatibility layer \u2014 Wine, and by extension Valve's Proton
      \u2014 rather than on\n native Windows. Detection runs once via Initialize
      during startup\n and the results are cached as static properties for cheap
      repeated reads."
    Remarks: "On non-Windows players (Android / Quest / Steam Frame native, Linux
      server) the\n Win32 probe is compiled out and every flag reports the native
      result:\n IsWine and IsProton are `false` and\n WineVersion is `null`. Reading
      any property auto-initializes,\n so call order is never load-bearing \u2014
      startup just primes the cache and logs once."
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
