    Summary: "A zero-length quaternion is entirely finite, so a component-wise IsFinite
      check calls it\n healthy \u2014 but Unity normalizes the rotation when it composes
      the matrix, so it yields a NaN\n world matrix for the transform and every descendant.
      Degeneracy has to be checked too, or\n the scan reports the victims and calls
      the writer's own bone \"ok\"."
