    Summary: "The same stage-tagged local-TRS scan, run over remote players instead:
      their avatar\n skeletons plus the mouth marker and nameplate, which are job-positioned
      scene roots of\n their own. Remote avatars share slot-indexed job state with
      the local one (the bone\n pipeline and jiggle both index parallel arrays),
      so a corrupt remote is both a first-class\n symptom and the usual way corruption
      reaches the local avatar \u2014 a local-only scan reports\n the wrong end of
      that. Budgeted by RemotePlayersPerCheckpoint."
    Remarks: 
