    Summary: "Caps skeleton-cache rebuilds per frame. A cache miss costs a\n `GetComponentsInChildren`
      over a whole avatar, and the checkpoints run dozens of times\n a frame \u2014
      so an avatar-swap burst (turning around reloads every far LOD at once) would\n
      otherwise turn every one of those calls into a hierarchy walk plus an allocation.
      A skipped\n player is simply visited on a later frame; the round-robin cursor
      already spreads coverage."
