    Summary: "Eye tracking, in one window.\n\n The pipeline view (which device is
      feeding gaze, how arbitration merges it, who consumes it)\n and the driver
      view (what the local eye driver does with that gaze) were separate windows,\n
      which meant diagnosing \"my eyes aren't moving\" involved opening both and
      guessing which half\n was at fault. Pipeline first: if no data arrives, the
      driver tab cannot help."
