  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.BasisSdk.Highlight.BasisHighlightOverride
    MemberName: BasisHighlightOverride
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: MonoBehaviour
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Per-renderer authoring for the BasisHighlight feature. Drop this on
      a\n GameObject with a Renderer to control how that renderer is drawn into the\n
      highlight mask when something highlights it via BasisHighlightManager:\n \n-
      BasisHighlightOverrideType.None \u2013 use the feature's\n   default/fallback
      mask (identical to having no component).\n- BasisHighlightOverrideType.Material
      \u2013 draw with\n   MaskMaterial, a silhouette shader matching this renderer's\n  
      geometry (e.g. one that reproduces a vertex deform so the outline lines up).\n-
      BasisHighlightOverrideType.Exclude \u2013 never highlight\n   this renderer,
      even while it is in the active set.\n\n The mode and material are inspector-serialized
      and also mutable at runtime\n via OverrideType / MaskMaterial; their setters\n
      re-register with the manager so the next frame's mask reflects the change.\n
      The renderer is cached in OnValidate so registration never\n reaches for GetComponent
      and stale references can't outlive the prefab."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
