  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.BasisSdk.Interactions.BasisHandGrip
    MemberName: BasisHandGrip
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Builds a hand frame from bone POSITIONS rather than from the hand bone's
      transform.\n\n The humanoid hand bone sits at the wrist and carries whatever
      bind orientation the avatar happened\n to be rigged with, so a grip expressed
      in it belongs to that one avatar: it seats objects behind the\n hand, and it
      does not survive being reconstructed against anybody else's rig. Joint positions
      carry\n no such convention \u2014 the palm, the direction down the hand and
      the axis across the knuckles mean the\n same thing on every humanoid. So a
      grip authored against this frame works on any avatar, and an\n observer showing
      a substitute avatar (fallback, still loading, performance level) reconstructs
      a held\n object into the hand it is actually drawing rather than into the geometry
      of the holder's."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
