    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Any player's hand frame off that player's own cached bone mapping \u2014
      the local player's rig driver\n or a remote's avatar driver, both of which
      the avatar drivers rebuild on every avatar change.\n Used by both ends of a
      networked hold so they agree without either sending rig data.\n\n Fails for
      a player that is neither, rather than answering with whatever rig happens to
      be lying\n around: the previous \"not remote, therefore local\" reading handed
      back the VIEWER'S OWN hand for\n any holder that had not resolved to a typed
      remote player yet (mid-join, mid-avatar-swap, a stale\n owner entry), which
      welds the held object into the hand of whoever is watching it."
