  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.BasisSdk.Interactions.BasisPhysicsSyncGate
    MemberName: BasisPhysicsSyncGate
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Coalesces the Physics.SyncTransforms calls owed by hand-moved colliders.\n
      \n\n`Physics.autoSyncTransforms` is off project-wide, so anything that repositions
      a collider\n by writing its transform has to flush before the next scene query
      or that collider keeps\n answering from its old pose. The flush is global:
      it walks every dirty collider transform in\n the scene, which on a populated
      instance is dominated by avatar and jiggle churn that has\n nothing to do with
      the caller. Calling it eagerly from a mover therefore pays the whole\n scene's
      bill every frame, including frames where nothing a query cares about actually
      moved.\n \n\n\n\n\n Movers call MarkColliderMoved instead, and the query that
      needs fresh colliders\n calls FlushIfDirty. One flush per frame at most, and
      none at all while the\n movers are idle."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
