    Summary: "True while this hold is actually driven by GripPoint \u2014 a welded
      hand hold whose\n grip solve succeeded, and past the pick-up ease so the object
      has arrived on it. The networked\n hold reads this before telling remotes to
      re-solve the grip from their own copy of the prefab:\n an authored GripPoint
      that the local hold never aligned to (weld off, a desktop grab, still\n easing
      in) would otherwise have every observer hold the object by a handle the owner
      is not."
