    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "VR weld source: when WeldToHand is enabled and a hand holds the object,
      returns the pose\n the object is welded to \u2014 the canonical hand frame
      from BasisHandGrip, anchored on the\n post-IK wrist so it tracks the rendered
      hand rather than the pre-IK target.\n\n The humanoid hand bone sits at the
      WRIST, so welding to it directly seats every object a palm-length\n behind
      the hand, sunk into the back of the wrist, and orients it by whatever bind
      rotation the avatar\n was rigged with. The hand frame is at the palm and built
      from joint positions instead.\n\n False for desktop (center-eye) holds, for
      an avatar the rig has no hand bone for, and before the first solve."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
