    Summary: "51 bone rotations in the RIG-NEUTRAL generic space: each joint's rotation
      away from its\n own rest pose, expressed in the CHARACTER's axes rather than
      in the sending rig's bone\n axes. That is what makes them genuinely avatar-agnostic
      \u2014 the receiver rebuilds its own\n rig's local rotations from them using
      only its own rest data, so a pose can be replayed\n on an avatar other than
      the one that produced it. See BasisGenericBoneRotation.\n Indexed by slot in
      BasisBoneRotationCompression.BONE_WRITE_ORDER."
