  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Platform.BasisDesktopFileDrop
    MemberName: BasisDesktopFileDrop
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The client's single OS file-drop bridge. On Windows players it subclasses
      the player window\n to intercept WM_DROPFILES; every dropped batch is queued
      and replayed from\n Dispatch on the main thread, where OnFilesDropped hands
      the raw\n paths to whoever wants them. Subscribers filter by extension themselves
      \u2014 images go to the\n image pickup manager, BEE files go to the library.\n\n
      There can only ever be one window subclass: the WndProc consumes the HDROP
      with DragFinish,\n so a second hook chained behind it would either see nothing
      or query freed native memory.\n That is why this lives in the framework rather
      than in whichever package wanted drops first.\n\n The native callbacks are
      static because IL2CPP cannot marshal instance-method delegates.\n Off Windows
      (and in the editor, where the player window hook cannot run) the install is
      a\n no-op, but the queue still works \u2014 the editor scene-view bridge feeds
      it through\n SubmitDroppedFiles so play-mode drops behave the same as shipped
      ones."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
