    Summary: "Drains queued drops and raises OnFilesDropped for each. Called once
      per\n frame from BasisEventDriver's central tick; a throwing subscriber is
      logged and skipped\n so it cannot take the rest of the batch \u2014 or the
      frame \u2014 down with it.\n\n Subscribers are invoked one at a time rather
      than through the multicast delegate: they\n are independent consumers of the
      same drop, and one of them throwing must not stop the\n others from seeing
      files that were theirs."
