    Summary: "Wall-clock ceiling on the swaps admitted per transmit tick. The count
      above bounds how\n many installs run, not what they cost \u2014 an install
      is a build plus a full remote\n calibration, and a heavy one drags the whole
      tick with it. This measures the swaps\n themselves (never the per-player flag
      reconciliation) and stops admitting more once the\n budget is gone; the rest
      stay pending and commit on later ticks, exactly as an exhausted\n count budget
      does."
