  - TypeFullName: BasisUrpQualityFields
    MemberName: BasisUrpQualityFields
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Reflection access to the handful of UniversalRenderPipelineAsset quality
      knobs\n URP exposes with a getter but an `internal` setter.\n\n \n\nThe alternative
      was widening those accessors in the embedded URP copy. Reflection keeps\n the
      fork surface at zero, so a URP package upgrade can't silently drop the change
      or land in\n conflict. The cost is that a rename becomes a runtime failure
      rather than a compile error,\n which is why every field is resolved once up
      front and a miss is logged loudly and then\n skipped \u2014 a missing knob
      must degrade to \"this tier doesn't lower that setting\", never to\n broken
      rendering.\n\n\n\nThe backing fields are written directly rather than through
      the property. Every one of\n these setters is a plain `m_X = value` passthrough
      with no side effects, so the two are\n equivalent \u2014 and going to the field
      also covers `enableLODCrossFade`, which has no setter\n at all. All six are
      `[SerializeField]`, so Unity's serializer keeps them and IL2CPP\n managed stripping
      won't remove them."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
