  - TypeFullName: BasisUserDataBackup
    MemberName: BasisUserDataBackup
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Packs everything this install keeps for the user into one portable
      archive, and unpacks it\n again on another machine.\n\n Two halves are covered:
      files under `Application.persistentDataPath` (settings, the avatar\n and item
      key stores, saved servers, trust lists, tracker pairings, per-player settings,
      input\n action bindings) and the `PlayerPrefs` entries that live outside persistentDataPath
      and so\n cannot be copied as files between machines (identity key pair, per-mode
      microphone setup,\n keyboard rebinds). The downloaded `BEEData` bundle cache
      is opt-in \u2014 the key stores alone\n are enough to pull the content down
      again, and the cache is often tens of gigabytes.\n\n The archive is an ordinary
      zip:\n ```\n\n   manifest.json          format version, timestamp, build, what
      was included\n   prefs.json             exported PlayerPrefs entries\n   data/<relative
      path>   mirror of the selected persistentDataPath tree\n \n```\n Root files
      are selected by extension minus an exclusion list rather than by a fixed list
      of\n names, so settings files added later are covered without touching this
      class. Subfolders are\n allow-listed, because most of them under persistentDataPath
      are recordings or debug dumps."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
