  - TypeFullName: 
    MemberName: ApplyMotionVectors
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Motion vectors are an extra per-frame pass over every renderer, and
      in stereo it runs\n per eye \u2014 so it is only worth paying for where something
      actually consumes\n `_MotionVectorTexture`.\n\n \n\nAndroid keeps them: Application
      SpaceWarp reprojects from app-supplied\n motion vectors, and `SpaceWarpFeature
      Android` is enabled in the OpenXR settings.\n\n\n\nStandalone does not. There
      is no Standalone SpaceWarp feature \u2014 PCVR\n reprojection (SteamVR Motion
      Smoothing, Oculus ASW over Link) runs in the compositor\n from its own history
      and does not read app motion vectors. Basis has no TAA either\n (`SMModuleAntialiasingURP`
      is MSAA-only), and the volumetric fog does no temporal\n reprojection. Re-enable
      this if STP is ever added to the antialiasing dropdown \u2014 STP is\n the
      one desktop consumer that would need them."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
