    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The physics hit lands on the COLLIDER face, which sits half the collider
      depth in front of\n the visual canvas plane (unit-scale world canvases: several
      real centimetres \u2014 the \"distance\n from the canvas\"). Snap the visual
      contact point along the ray onto the canvas plane so the\n line tip and reticle
      touch the panel the user actually sees, whatever the collider depth\n convention.
      Falls back to the raw hit when no canvas is resolved or the geometry is odd."
    Remarks: 
