  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.UI.
    MemberName: TryGetPanelPosition
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 5
    ParamNames:
    - ray
    - requireInsideBounds
    - panelPosition
    - worldPosition
    - distance
    ParamDocs:
    - "False while a press is captured, so a drag that leaves the panel keeps feeding\n
      coordinates instead of freezing (UI Toolkit clamps sliders itself)."
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Converts a world-metre thickness into the panel's local units.\n\n
      The collider's width and height come straight from the panel size, so they
      are in panel\n units \u2014 the depth has to be expressed in the same space
      or the box is inconsistent.\n Writing metres in directly made the collider
      vanishingly thin once the transform was\n scaled down (0.02 became ~10 microns
      on the camera deck), which turns every ray hit\n into a grazing one and leaves
      the fingertip nothing to press into.\n\n uGUI uses the same convention: BasisGraphicUIRayCaster
      sizes canvas colliders entirely\n in canvas units, so depth scales with the
      canvas rather than staying a fixed metre value."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
