  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.
    MemberName: OnDestroy
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - ReleaseInstance(false
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 1
    Summary: "`dropFromLayout` deactivates the object before releasing it.\n BasisAddressablePrefabCache.DestroyInstance
      destroys via\n Object.Destroy, which Unity defers to the end of the frame,
      so a released\n element otherwise stays an active child and keeps contributing
      to its parent layout\n group for the rest of this frame \u2014 the layout then
      lands wrong for exactly one frame\n (visible when a lazy tab replaces its placeholder).
      Deactivating applies immediately and\n drops it out of that pass. Skipped when
      the release is already being driven by\n OnDestroy, where changing active state
      is not valid."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.BasisAddressablePrefabCache
    MemberName: BasisAddressablePrefabCache
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Loads each UI prefab through Addressables once and instantiates plain
      clones from then on,\n instead of paying an Addressables handle + location
      lookup per element. Menu pages build\n dozens-to-hundreds of elements from
      a handful of prefab paths, so this removes almost all\n of the per-element
      load cost.\n \n\n\n Instances created here are plain UnityEngine.Object.Instantiate(UnityEngine.Object)\n
      clones, which Addressables.ReleaseInstance(GameObject) does NOT destroy \u2014
      release\n paths must call DestroyInstance instead or every released element
      leaks."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
