  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.
    MemberName: RebuildLayoutChain
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 2
    ParamNames:
    - from
    - LayoutRebuilder.ForceRebuildLayoutImmediate(current
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Rebuilds outward from a container whose contents just changed height,
      hitting every ancestor\n that actually carries a layout controller, innermost
      first, so each outer pass sees the\n corrected inner height. Rows revealed
      or hidden inside a nested group otherwise leave every\n group above them at
      its stale height \u2014 the group keeps the size it had, so the rows below
      it\n never move and the page looks like it ignored the toggle. Rebuilding the
      page root instead\n does not fix it: that pass measures the inner group before
      the group has resized itself.\n \n\n\n Stops at `stopAt` \u2014 pass the tab
      page's content so one reveal does not\n rebuild the whole menu."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
