  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.BasisPanelMoveHandle
    MemberName: BasisPanelMoveHandle
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: MonoBehaviour
    Interfaces:
    - IPointerDownHandler
    - IPointerUpHandler
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The move control for a panel, along with the reset that sits beside
      it. Holding move drags\n the panel around with whatever is pointing at it \u2014
      the mouse on desktop, a hand ray in VR \u2014\n and in VR the thumbstick of
      the hand doing the holding reels the panel closer or pushes it\n away. Desktop
      drags stay in the panel's own plane and inside the screen: there is no depth\n
      axis to aim along with a mouse, and a panel dragged off the edge could not
      be dragged back.\n \n\n\n Where the user leaves it is remembered per panel
      and per platform, see\n BasisPanelOffsetMemory. Reset puts it back where the
      panel was authored, and\n keeps out of the way until there is something to
      put back.\n \n\n\n\n\n The drag is computed entirely in the panel parent's
      local space. On desktop both the pointer\n and the menu follow the head, so
      a world-space delta would count that shared motion twice and\n the panel would
      slide away whenever the user turned."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
