  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.BasisPanelResetGesture
    MemberName: BasisPanelResetGesture
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Reset-to-default gesture for panel elements: while hovering a control,
      a right-click\n (desktop) or a thumbstick click (VR) asks to reset it. Both
      are polled rather than handled\n as pointer buttons, because `BasisUIInput`
      never fills its right-button state (so a\n right-click produces no UI pointer
      event at all) and a thumbstick click is not a pointer\n button in the first
      place.\n\n \n\n\n Only the device whose pointer is on the control is listened
      to. The other hand's stick is\n that hand's own pointer, and far more often
      it is walking or snap-turning; a control under\n one ray must not answer the
      stick of the hand doing something else entirely.\n \n\n\n\n\n It is a click,
      not a press: the reset runs on release, and only when the press both started\n
      and ended on the same control with the same device, within MaxClickHoldSeconds.\n
      A stick pushed and held \u2014 locomotion, or a panel drag \u2014 is not a
      click and never resets.\n \n\n\n\n Only one element can be hovered at a time,
      so the poll lives here as a single frame-clock\n subscription held for the
      duration of that hover, instead of an Update on every control."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
