    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Moves the slider's upper bound after creation, for ceilings that can
      change while the\n panel is up (see BasisAudioRangeSliderLimit). Only the range
      and its\n labels are touched \u2014 a full SetSliderSettings would also rewrite
      the title\n and description, which callers commonly set after the settings.\n
      \n\n\n A lowered bound clamps the handle but is deliberately never written
      back to the settings\n binding: whoever consumes the value caps it themselves,
      so raising the ceiling again has\n to restore the choice the user actually
      made."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
