  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Device_Management.BasisTrackerMarkerGizmos
    MemberName: BasisTrackerMarkerGizmos
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The player-facing tracker \"marker\" balls \u2014 the generic placeholder
      visual for tracked\n devices (the Markers tracker-visuals mode, and the fallback
      whenever a runtime device\n model is unavailable). Drawn through the batched
      gizmo backend instead of a FallbackSphere\n GameObject per device: each registered
      input gets a solid, lit, depth-tested ball using\n the FallbackSphere prefab's
      own material, scaled with avatar height exactly like the old\n BasisVisualTracker
      (\xD8 0.05 \xD7 height ratio). The per-frame tick recomputes the pose the\n
      device transform will render with this frame (ScaledDeviceCoord + playspace
      flip, applied\n later in AfterSimulateOnRender) so the ball never trails the
      avatar. Ticked from\n BasisEventDriver just before the gizmo submission; gizmo
      ids are lazily re-created after\n the debug-gizmo master teardown wipes the
      manager."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
