  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Device_Management.EyeTracking.BasisGazeFoveationAutoDriver
    MemberName: BasisGazeFoveationAutoDriver
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Drives gaze-foveated VRS automatically from eye-tracking presence:\n
      - When an eye-tracking headset is first detected, asks once (per headset) to
      enable it.\n - Remembers the answer per headset and applies it silently thereafter.\n
      - Turns VR VRS off when the eye-tracking headset goes away (doffed / switched
      to desktop /\n   swapped to a non-eye-tracking headset).\n\n It only manages
      VR VRS in response to eye tracking it turned on \u2014 it never forces a user's\n
      manual VR/desktop VRS choice off on its own. Pumped from the central tick;
      no MonoBehaviour."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
