    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Whether the player has gone quiet long enough to hand their OpenLipSync
      slot to\n somebody closer. Judged from TrackedAudioSource, which is the player's\n
      SPATIAL source \u2014 so a announcer, who sends on the announce channel and therefore
      never\n feeds that source at all, reads as idle while mid-sentence. Releasing
      then is not\n merely wasteful: `ProcessAudioSamples` immediately asks for the
      context back, so\n the driver churns a fresh context every frame and the buffered
      audio is discarded\n before inference ever sees it, which shows up as a mouth
      that never moves."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
