  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Drivers.BasisHandPoseGrid
    MemberName: BasisHandPoseGrid
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: IDisposable
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The baked map from a hand's twenty-scalar input (five curl/splay pairs
      per hand, which is what\n every Basis finger backend reduces to) onto that
      avatar's thirty finger joint rotations.\n\n Split out of BasisLocalHandDriver
      so a REMOTE player can run the identical reconstruction. The\n sampler below
      is the single copy of the interpolation \u2014 local and remote must agree
      bit for\n bit, or the hand a player sees on themselves is not the hand everyone
      else sees, and the\n remote apply path's write mask (which skips a transform
      write when the composed rotation is\n unchanged) stops firing on settled fingers.\n\n
      The grid is a property of the AVATAR ASSET, not of the player wearing it, so
      it is interned\n through BasisAvatarModelCache: a crowd in matching avatars
      bakes once."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
