  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Drivers.
    MemberName: DisposeOwnedOnly
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - Cells.Dispose(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Teardown for a driver that is going away: frees cells this grid OWNS
      and leaves a\n shared view completely alone."
    Remarks: "Deliberately does NOT clear a view the way Dispose does. The parallel\n
      network compute samples this grid from worker threads and is only guaranteed
      joined at\n a few points in the frame; nulling Cells from a teardown that can
      run\n outside those windows is a torn read. Leaving the view costs nothing
      \u2014 the shared\n buffer outlives the cache entry by design, and a destroyed
      player is off the receiver\n snapshot so nothing samples it again."
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
