  - TypeFullName: ObservedBodySize
    MemberName: ObservedBodySize
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Takes the best measurement seen while the player has actually been
      using the world, in place of\n whatever a single capture happened to catch.\n\n
      Adoption is a simple \"keep the larger\", which is not a heuristic but the
      same argument the rest\n of this file rests on: a slouch, a crouch or arms
      at your sides all read SHORT, and nothing\n short of a tracking glitch reads
      longer than the body actually is. So between two measurements\n of one unchanging
      body, the longer is the better one \u2014 and the sampler has thousands of
      chances\n to catch the player upright and reaching where a single capture had
      one."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
