  - TypeFullName: 
    MemberName: ResolveHeightMode
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - BasisSelectedHeightMode.Auto
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Resolves BasisSelectedHeightMode.Auto. In VR it becomes\n BasisSelectedHeightMode.BestFit:
      rather than picking whichever single measurement\n looks most trustworthy and
      letting the other one be wrong, the fit uses every measurement at\n once and
      hands the leftover to the positional stretcher. Desktop always resolves to
      EyeHeight \u2014\n its hands are not the player's hands and its eye height
      is a synthesized number, so there is\n nothing to fit against. Concrete modes
      pass through untouched."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
