  - TypeFullName: 
    MemberName: SolveUniformScale
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Chooses the single uniform scale that fits the player into the avatar
      best, from every body\n measurement held, and records what each segment has
      left over for the positional stretcher.\n\n Reads the AUTHORED avatar measurements
      only \u2014 never the post-fit ones \u2014 so it can run before the\n stretcher
      and hand it a fixed target. Each limb tells the solver how many avatar-metres
      of\n mismatch the stretcher could absorb for it (BasisBodyFitCore.ArmSpanSlack
      and\n friends, so the two agree by construction); while every limb stays inside
      its budget the scale\n matches eye height exactly and the stretcher does all
      the work.\n\n Leaves AppliedUniformScale at 0 for every mode but BestFit, which
      makes the body\n fit fall back to the eye-height ratio it has always used.
      The concrete modes are manual\n overrides and arm-span mode in particular is
      degenerate here (its scale is derived from the\n post-fit span, so scale and
      fit define each other); BestFit is the mode where the question is\n well posed,
      and it is what Auto now resolves to."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
