  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Drivers.BasisLocalPlayspaceMover
    MemberName: BasisLocalPlayspaceMover
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Lets a VR user grab and drag (and optionally rotate/scale) their play
      space by holding a\n configurable controller input, the way naelstrof's VRPlayspaceMover
      does. Gated behind the\n Body Tracking \"Playspace Mover\" toggle and driven
      each frame after character movement.\n\n Horizontal (X/Z) drag is applied incrementally
      through the character controller, so it composes\n with normal locomotion instead
      of blocking it and still resolves walls/floors. One held hand\n drags (translation).
      Two hands holding the main input scale (drives the custom avatar scale, not\n
      the play space); two hands holding the rotation input rotate (yaw). The net
      horizontal drag is\n tracked so ResetOffset can undo it while leaving normal
      locomotion intact.\n\n Vertical (Y) drag works like OVR Advanced Settings'
      \"Space Drag\": you pull yourself up or down\n and stay where you let go. It
      can't ride the character controller (gravity, applied earlier in\n the frame,
      would claw it straight back), so instead it accumulates into VerticalOffset\n
      \u2014 a tracking-space height offset injected into every device in\n Device_Management.Devices.BasisInput.ComputeUnscaledDeviceCoord,
      the same hook seated\n mode uses for its height delta. That shifts the whole
      tracking space (view, hands, avatar) without\n moving the capsule or touching
      gravity, so it persists for free. Gated by the \"Vertical\" toggle."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
