  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Drivers.BasisRemoteAudioDriver
    MemberName: OwnsVisemeTap
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - driver
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Whether this driver may feed the shared viseme analyser this callback.\n
      \n\nWhile a player announces, TWO AudioSources point at the same\n BasisAudioAndVisemeDriver:
      the announce source carrying their voice, and\n their own spatial source, which
      receives nothing (a announcer transmits on the announce\n channel only) and therefore
      writes a buffer of silence every callback. Feeding both\n splices that silence
      through the mel front-end between real speech \u2014 poisoning the\n streaming
      convolution caches the model carries between hops \u2014 and races the analyser's\n
      ingest buffer, which is written assuming a single producer. So the announce source
      takes\n the tap on its own for as long as the announce lasts.\n\n\n\nOwnership
      is a match between the source's kind and the player's current mode\n rather
      than \"announce wins\": that makes it exactly one owner in BOTH directions off
      a\n single volatile read, so the teardown window \u2014 where the announce driver
      still holds a\n live viseme driver for the rest of the frame, because Object.Destroy
      is deferred \u2014\n cannot briefly double up."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
