  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Drivers.
    MemberName: SetBodyFit
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - ApplyRemoteBodyFit(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Places the nameplate and mouth markers on the pose the bone jobs will
      give them next\n frame. Both are standalone scene roots created at world origin
      by\n BasisRemotePlayer.RemoteInitialize and only ever moved by\n MappedNameplateApplyJob
      / ApplyMouthJob at the tail of\n LateUpdate, so a joining player's plate renders
      at (0,0,0) for the frame their avatar\n installs on \u2014 the avatar itself
      no longer does, which leaves the plate alone out there.\n\n The plate goes
      through the same BasisNamePlateAnchorMath.AnchorWorldY and\n the same yaw-only
      billboard the apply job uses, so the two cannot drift apart. The mouth\n takes
      the head bone's world pose: its real anchor is that pose plus the authored\n
      centimetre-scale offset, it carries no renderer, and reproducing the head-chain
      FK here\n would duplicate the job for a marker nobody sees."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
