  - TypeFullName: HeadChainLink
    MemberName: HeadChainLink
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "One step of the baked hips\u2192head chain that lets the head world
      pose be composed from data the\n pipeline already owns, instead of read back
      off the transform a frame late.\n\n Each link covers exactly one SYNCED bone
      plus any static nodes above it (twist/roll bones,\n Armature-style intermediates),
      folded into a single offset + pre-rotation. That keeps the walk\n as short
      as the number of synced bones in the chain \u2014 5 on a standard humanoid
      (Spine, Chest,\n UpperChest, Neck, Head, which are BONE_WRITE_ORDER slots 0..4)
      \u2014 no matter how many extra nodes\n a rig puts between them."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
