  - TypeFullName: 
    MemberName: AuthoringLength
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames:
    - boneTransforms
    ParamDocs:
    - "The bone array ONLY if the skeleton is actually being registered for this
      avatar \u2014 callers\n must pass null under exactly the condition that fills
      the skeleton slots with dummies.\n A bone whose transform is never written
      is a static node to this walk, and treating it as\n driven would pose the head
      off rotations that never reach the rig."
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Registrations deferred out of the avatar-load path and committed at
      the top of\n Schedule. Adding to the SoA/TAA mid-frame forces a job sync; folding
      the\n commits into the sync the frame already does removes that per-add stall,
      which is what\n hits when many avatars calibrate in the same window (e.g. a
      large simultaneous join).\n Removal stays synchronous in RemoveRemotePlayer:
      teardown must drop the TAA\n entry while the transform is still alive (Unity
      auto-removes destroyed transforms from a\n TransformAccessArray, which would
      desync the parallel SoA), so it can't be deferred."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
