  - TypeFullName: 
    MemberName: ScheduleHipsDerive
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - 0
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Kicks the hips fan-out + root derive + head FK at the earliest point
      it is legal: straight\n after the per-receiver loop. That loop is a genuine
      ordering constraint \u2014\n `SetFilteredHipsOverride` writes the very `_filteredPositions`
      slots this job reads\n (see the seat/vehicle path) \u2014 but nothing after
      it is, so waiting for Schedule() was pure\n main-thread latency.\n\n This is
      also why the head FK lives here rather than in the skeleton decode: the head
      hangs\n off the hips pose, so it has to see the overrides, and the decode is
      deliberately kicked\n AHEAD of the receiver loop where they aren't final yet."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
