    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Exposes the SoA index \u2192 player ID reverse map so a job can walk
      the dense slot range\n itself instead of the main thread resolving one index
      per receiver. Only the first\n AuthoringLength entries are live; the tail holds
      stale keys after a\n removal. Returns a default (uncreated) array when the
      system isn't initialized.\n\n Valid for the current frame only \u2014 the backing
      array is reallocated when the player\n count grows, so callers must re-acquire
      it rather than cache it, exactly as with\n GetRemoteFrameArray."
    Remarks: 
