  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Networking.Sync.Testing.BasisSyncLatency
    MemberName: BasisSyncLatency
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Measures END-TO-END LATENCY of the generic value-sync path \u2014 the
      wall-clock gap between the\n owner writing a value and a remote rendering it.
      This is the \"why does it feel laggy\" axis the\n convergence matrix (BasisSyncSim)
      deliberately leaves out: that harness freezes the\n signal and asks \"does
      the remote eventually reach the final value\"; this one keeps the signal\n
      moving and asks \"how far behind is the remote at every frame\".\n\n Method:
      a single continuous field is driven by a LINEAR RAMP (value = slope\xB7t),
      so the remote's\n interpolated output inverts cleanly back to the owner time
      that produced it, and\n latency = now \u2212 value/slope. It drives the REAL
      BasisSyncReceiver through the REAL\n SimSender cadence and SimNetwork wire
      (same primitives the convergence\n harness uses), so the number reflects shipping
      code, not a re-implementation.\n\n Distance reduction (default ON for synced
      objects) is modeled here because it is a first-order\n latency contributor
      in practice: the owner throttles its send rate by squared distance to the\n
      nearest observer, and the jitter buffer then holds 2+ of those now-larger intervals
      \u2014 so latency\n grows roughly quadratically with viewer distance."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
