  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Networking.Voice.Testing.
    MemberName: FindNotches
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 7
    ParamNames:
    - mono
    - sampleRate
    - 0.4
    - 25.0
    - 3.0
    - 0.004f
    - 0.03f
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Finds underrun-style notches: runs of near-silence between\n `minMs`
      and `maxMs` long whose flanks\n (within `flankMs` on both sides) carry real
      signal.\n Long gaps (word pauses, mutes) are ignored by the max-length bound.\n
      The flank window is deliberately tight: an underrun fade cuts from full\n amplitude
      to digital silence within ~2 ms, so real notches have loud\n IMMEDIATE neighbours.
      Additionally the dip must contain a run of true\n digital-zero samples \u2014
      the underrun path writes exact 0s once its fade\n lands, whereas codec-shaped
      speech (a gain-quantized syllable trough or a\n decaying utterance tail) merely
      OSCILLATES through zero and never rests\n there. Without the zero-run requirement
      those codec artifacts, which are\n masked and inaudible, would count as playback
      faults."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
