  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Networking.Voice.Testing.BasisVoiceSignal
    MemberName: BasisVoiceSignal
    Kind: Enum
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Offline, deterministic exerciser for the voice pipeline:\n mic frames
      -> REAL Opus encode (same CTLs as `BasisAudioTransmission`) ->\n REAL AudioSegmentDataMessage
      wire serialize -> simulated server relay\n (mirrors `HandleVoiceMessage`/`SendVoiceMessageToClients`:
      deserialize, wrap in a REAL\n ServerAudioSegmentMessage, serialize once) ->
      seeded network impairments\n (latency / jitter / loss / bursts / stalls) ->
      REAL BasisAudioReceiver\n (jitter buffer, FEC/PLC, idle reset, adaptive depth,
      fades, resampler, limiter) pulled\n on a virtual audio clock. The rendered
      output is scored against the input signal and a\n codec-only baseline, so network/timing
      damage separates from inherent Opus loss.\n\n Out of scope (needs a live client):
      the AudioSource enable/disable state machine,\n Steam Audio spatialization,
      mic-device capture, and the recipient/range filtering\n (the sim assumes the
      listener is in range the whole run)."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
