  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.BasisSdk.Interactions.
    MemberName: TryGetHandSearchPosition
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 2
    ParamNames:
    - hand
    - 1
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Where a hand grab searches from. The humanoid hand bone sits at the
      WRIST, so searching\n there means reaching with the back of the hand \u2014
      visibly behind the palm. The middle\n finger's proximal knuckle marks the far
      side of the palm, and the midpoint of the two\n reads as \"in my hand\".\n\n
      Both bones come straight off the rig driver's cached BasisTransformMapping,\n
      which the avatar driver already rebuilds on every avatar change \u2014 no bone
      lookups and no\n cache of our own to invalidate. The debug gizmo calls this
      same method, so the drawn pick\n sphere can never sit somewhere the search
      does not."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
