  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.BasisSdk.Interactions.BasisJiggleTouchLatch
    MemberName: BasisJiggleTouchLatch
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Turns a per-frame \"is this hand on the chain\" answer into begin and
      end events.\n\n A hand resting on a chain sits right at the edge of the grip
      volume and drops contact for the\n odd frame, so raw contact would fire a callback
      storm into sandboxed script. The two edges are\n deliberately not symmetric:
      a touch begins the instant contact is made, because a\n delayed reaction feels
      broken, while it only ends once the loss of contact has persisted\n for the
      dwell. Any contact inside that window cancels the pending release, so flicker
      collapses\n to a single begin and a single end.\n\n Rate-limiting the edges
      instead \u2014 refusing to change state within the dwell of the last change\n
      \u2014 reads as equivalent and is not: with contact alternating every frame
      it still flips as soon\n as enough time has accrued, which is a storm at half
      the frame rate."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
