  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.BasisSdk.Interactions.BasisJiggleGrabPicker
    MemberName: BasisJiggleGrabPicker
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Chooses which jiggle point a grab press takes. Kept as pure geometry
      with no scene, player\n or network dependency so the selection rules can be
      tested directly \u2014 the accuracy problems\n worth catching here are all
      \"it picked the wrong point\", which is a maths question.\n\n Two shapes of
      query, deliberately scored differently:\n\n \u2022 Grasp \u2014 a capsule from
      the palm to the fingertips rather than a sphere at the palm,\n   because a
      hand closes around what lies across its fingers. A sphere centred on the palm\n  
      both misses a strand resting on the fingers and grabs one floating behind the
      knuckles.\n   Nearest to the segment wins, so among several strands in the
      hand you get the one you are\n   actually touching.\n\n \u2022 Point \u2014
      an exact perpendicular distance to the aim ray, not a march of overlapping\n  
      spheres. Marching made the result depend on the step size and let a point that
      merely sat\n   near an early sample beat one dead on the axis. Distance along
      the ray dominates the score\n   so the nearest thing you point at wins, with
      off-axis distance as the tiebreak."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
