  - TypeFullName: LocalOpusSettings
    MemberName: PacketLossPercent
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Expected packet loss percentage used to tune Opus's in-band Forward
      Error\n Correction (OPUS_SET_PACKET_LOSS_PERC). Higher values spend more bitrate\n
      on redundant FEC data embedded in each packet, giving the decoder a better\n
      chance of reconstructing a single-packet loss via decode_fec=true. Valid\n
      range is 0..100; Opus recommends ~10 for moderate networks and up to ~30\n
      for lossy ones. Set to 0 to effectively disable FEC. ~15% bitrate overhead\n
      at the default value.\n\n Prefer SetPacketLossPercent for runtime changes so
      live encoders\n pick up the new value via OnPacketLossPercentChanged."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
