  - TypeFullName: 
    MemberName: HandleOwnershipTransfer
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - HandleOwnership(OwnershipTransferMessage
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Replays messages that arrived before their handler existed, in the
      order they arrived.\n\n This used to walk the list backwards \u2014 safe for
      removal during iteration, but it delivered newest\n first, which silently reverses
      the wire order the transport went to the trouble of guaranteeing. For\n anything
      sent as a sequence that is fatal rather than untidy: an image pickup joining
      an instance\n received every chunk of a transfer before the spawn header that
      opens it, so the chunks were dropped\n as belonging to no transfer, the header
      then raised a card with nothing left to fill it, and the card\n was removed
      thirty seconds later when the transfer timed out. Handlers registering during
      a replay is\n also legal, so the list is settled before anything is invoked."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
