  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Networking.NetworkedAvatar.BasisAvatarEndEffectors
    MemberName: BasisAvatarEndEffectors
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Wire codec for the end-effector anchoring block (High quality only,
      appended after the tail).\n\n Layout \u2014 35 bytes = 280 bits, LSB-first
      via BasisBoneRotationCompression.WriteBits:\n   [mask : 8 bits]  bit0 LHand,
      bit1 RHand, bit2 LFoot, bit3 RFoot (1 = anchored / valid)\n   4 \xD7 effector,
      each 68 bits:\n     [tip position : 3 \xD7 12 bits]  hips-local offset in a
      \xB12 m box  (~1 mm)\n     [tip rotation : 2 + 3\xD710 bits] smallest-three
      world orientation (~0.08\xB0)\n\n A per-effector 8-bit swivel (elbow/knee pole
      angle) used to follow the rotation. It was dropped\n because the receiver stopped
      reading it: the pole is taken from the FK joint position instead,\n which is
      stable and has no reference-axis degeneracy (see BasisRemoteNetworkDriver's
      solve).\n\n The block is fixed-size regardless of the mask so reads stay fixed-offset;
      unanchored slots are\n simply ignored by the receiver. Positions are hips-local
      so they inherit the hips' precision and\n need no absolute-world range. See
      BasisRemoteLimbIK for how the receiver applies them."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
