  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Networking.NetworkedAvatar.BasisBoneDeltaAndCompressJob
    MemberName: BasisBoneDeltaAndCompressJob
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: IJob
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Burst-compiled job that converts bone local rotations into the rig-neutral
      generic\n rotation space and compresses them into a packed byte buffer using
      smallest-three\n quaternion encoding.\n\n Replaces the main-thread ExtractBoneDeltas()
      + CompressBoneRotations() calls\n with a single Burst-optimized pass. The job
      reads current bone local rotations\n (written by a prior TransformAccessArray
      read), maps them into generic space with the\n folded operators cached at calibration,
      and writes the compressed bitstream.\n\n The mapped value is `g = pre * currentLocal
      * post` \u2014 see\n Basis.Network.Core.Compression.BasisGenericBoneRotation
      for what g means and\n why the operators fold this way. Conjugation preserves
      rotation angle, so g occupies\n exactly the same magnitude range the old T-pose-relative
      local delta did and the\n smallest-three budget below is unchanged.\n\n This
      runs as an IJob (not parallel) because the bit-packed output is sequential.\n
      Burst still provides significant wins via SIMD quaternion math and branch elimination."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
