    Summary: "Fills slot-order decode tables from per-bone arrays indexed by HumanBodyBones
      enum value\n (the shape BasisAvatarModelCache caches, so a repeat instance
      of a known avatar skips\n the dictionary walk entirely).\n\n `bonePresent`
      gates each slot: a bone the rig does not have gets the\n legacy identity-rest
      pair, which composes the incoming generic value straight onto the\n (unused)
      rest local rather than through a meaningless frame.\n\n `restFrameByBone` holds
      RAW root-space rest rotations (what the cache\n stores); `characterBasis` is
      what turns them into the shared frame, so\n it must be the basis measured for
      the SAME avatar those rotations came from."
