    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "While held, the transform channels carry the prop's offset from the
      holder's hand rather than a world\n pose, so every axis has to be synced: a
      disabled one drops that component of the grip and the prop\n sits wrong on
      every other client, permanently, while looking perfect to the holder \u2014
      who never decodes\n what it sent. Free-flying props can legitimately sync a
      subset, which is why this warns rather than\n forcing the axes back on."
