  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Networking.Receivers.BasisAudioRemoteSource
    MemberName: MaxPoolSize
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "How many voice objects to keep parked for reuse. Sized for the audible
      crowd, not for\n a handful of speakers: a miss is dramatically more expensive
      than a hit, and in a busy\n instance the in/out-of-hearing-range set churns
      continuously."
    Remarks: "A hit is `SetParent` + `SetActive`. A miss Instantiates the prefab,
      which\n runs Steam Audio's native source creation and \u2014 because `UnityAudioEngineSource`\n
      wipes its parameter cache to NaN on Initialize \u2014 pushes all 31 spatializer
      parameters,\n each one a DSP graph mutation. A pooled object keeps its audio
      engine source alive\n across the disable (only OnDestroy tears it down) and
      its parameter hash unchanged, so\n reuse pushes none of them. At 16 this pool
      was smaller than a single join burst, so\n every start paid the miss."
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
