  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Networking.Receivers.
    MemberName: BoneTransforms
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Folded operators that turn the incoming RIG-NEUTRAL bone rotations
      into THIS avatar's\n bone local rotations: `localRotation = BoneDecodePre[slot]
      * generic * BoneDecodePost[slot]`.\n Slot order is BasisBoneRotationCompression.BONE_WRITE_ORDER.\n\n
      Built during calibration from this rig's own rest pose \u2014 see\n Basis.Network.Core.Compression.BasisGenericBoneRotation.
      Because they are\n derived purely from the LOCAL avatar's rest data, the sender's
      rig never enters into it,\n which is what lets any incoming pose play back
      on whatever avatar is worn here.\n Passed to RemoteBoneJobSystem for the skeleton
      compose job."
    Remarks: 
