    Summary: "Catmull-Rom rotation of the p1->p2 segment at t in [0,1].\n The four
      quaternions are hemisphere-aligned to p1 first (so the spline\n takes the short
      way and is immune to the codec's sign canonicalization),\n interpolated component-wise,
      then renormalized. Cheaper than a true\n SQUAD and visually indistinguishable
      at network step sizes."
