  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Networking.Receivers.BasisVoiceAcoustics
    MemberName: BasisVoiceAcoustics
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The acoustic model for a remote player's voice: how loud they are at
      a\n distance, how their mouth radiates, and how much of them the listener's\n
      own head is in the way of.\n\n Everything here is pure math over floats so
      it can be unit tested without\n the audio engine. The numbers come from fitting
      three published data sets:\n Chu & Warnock (NRC RR-104) for talker directivity,
      the direct+diffuse\n field split for distance, and head/torso diffraction for
      the listener cone.\n\n What each piece replaces:\n  \u2022 DistanceGain replaces
      a hand-drawn rolloff curve that was\n    flat to ~6 m and then fell off a cliff.
      It measured 8.3 dB RMS away from\n    a real talker over 0.5-15 m and gave
      only 21 % of the real level change\n    between 1 m and 4 m, which is why everyone
      sounded equally close.\n  \u2022 DirectivityShelfDb supplies the spectral tilt
      that Steam\n    Audio's dipole cannot: a real mouth turned away loses ~12 dB
      more at\n    4 kHz than at 250 Hz, while a broadband dipole only gets quieter.\n 
      \u2022 ListenerConeTerms keeps the cone-of-influence feature but\n    spends
      most of it above HeadShadowCornerHz, so a talker\n    behind you reads as occluded
      rather than as a fader being pulled."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Networking.Receivers.BasisVoiceAcoustics
    MemberName: DistanceTaperStart
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 1
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Fraction of the hearing range at which the curve starts tapering to\n
      zero. Purely so the hearing-range cull is silent \u2014 the source is\n hard-stopped
      at maxDistance and released at 1.1x that, so the curve has\n to already be
      inaudible there. 0.95 puts the level at the cull radius\n near -58 dB while
      leaving the rest of the range undistorted."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
