  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Networking.Receivers.BasisVoiceToneShaper
    MemberName: BasisVoiceToneShaper
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Two cascaded one-pole high shelves applied to a remote voice on the
      audio\n thread: one for the talker's mouth directivity, one for the listener's
      own\n head being in the way. Together they carry the frequency-dependent part
      of\n the spatial model \u2014 the part Unity's distance rolloff and Steam Audio's\n
      broadband dipole structurally cannot express.\n\n Each shelf is `H(z) = g +
      (1-g)\xB7LP(z)`: unity below the corner,\n exactly `g` above it, 4 ops per
      sample and no allocation. Both shelf\n gains are ramped across the callback,
      because the angles driving them move\n every time either head turns and a per-callback
      step would zipper."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
