    Summary: "Frames several synced objects' update payloads into one scene-data
      packet so a client owning many\n objects amortizes the per-packet header +
      transport overhead. Each entry is [NetworkID u16][len u16][payload];\n the
      reader walks entries until the buffer is exhausted (the scene-data length bounds
      it). Because one packet\n carries a single delivery method and recipient set,
      only objects that match on both can share a batch."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
