  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Networking.Sync.BasisSyncBatchCollector
    MemberName: BasisSyncBatchCollector
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "EXPERIMENTAL, off by default. Coalesces a client's owned scene-data
      sends into fewer packets to amortize the\n per-packet header + transport overhead.
      Only broadcast (no explicit recipients), server-relayed (non-P2P-direct)\n
      sends are batched; everything else falls back to an individual send.\n\n Enabling
      is a SESSION-WIDE policy: it changes the wire framing for batched objects,
      so every client must agree,\n and BatchMessageIndex must never be assigned
      to a real networked object (reserve it in the id\n allocator) \u2014 otherwise
      it collides with that object's receive handler. Verify a real batched round-trip
      before\n shipping it on."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
