      the transport\n can fragment. False for everything that fits one datagram,
      which is the case that matters: a normal\n synced object's packet is tens of
      bytes against a ~1 KB budget, so this adds nothing to the wire and\n leaves
      the requested delivery exactly as configured. Pure and internal so that stays
      a pinned\n property rather than a claim."
