  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Networking.Sync.BasisSyncedTransform
    MemberName: BasisSyncedTransform
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: BasisSyncedObject
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Drop-in transform sync built on BasisSyncedObject. The owner streams
      the enabled\n axes; every other client's copy is interpolated and composed
      each frame \u2014 off the main thread by\n the Burst apply job unless the configuration
      needs it (RelativeTo, or a subclass overriding\n ApplyInterpolated). Per-axis
      toggles let\n you sync only what moves (e.g. a door = rotation Y only in Euler
      mode), the rotation mode picks the\n orientation encoding (smallest-three /
      quaternion / Euler), uniform scale streams one value to all axes,\n per-axis
      compression (Half / Ranged) shrinks the float cost, and teleport-threshold
      tunes late packets.\n\n For custom values use the code API on BasisSyncedObject
      directly\n (RegisterFloat / RegisterColor / RegisterUShort / ... then LocalSet
      / RemoteGet)."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
