  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Networking.VoiceRecording.BasisVoiceTapSink
    MemberName: BasisVoiceTapSink
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Thread-safe ring for decoded mono PCM feeding the recording path (NOT
      the playback\n path). Decode threads call Write; the main thread drains with\n
      Drain. A player can be decoded by both a normal and a announce receiver on\n independent
      audio threads during a mode transition, so this must tolerate multiple\n producers
      \u2014 a short lock guards the cursors and slots. The lock is only ever taken
      by\n the recording side-tap, never by voice playback, so it cannot degrade
      audio output.\n On overflow (the consumer stalled) the newest samples are dropped
      and counted."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
