  - TypeFullName: 
    MemberName: Warm
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - cache.ContainsKey(Sanitize(uuid))
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Fire-and-forget cache fill for a UUID that is about to be requested
      several times.\n A joining player is asked for by the avatar loader, the jiggle
      collider setup and the\n nameplate's block state; warming from the avatar load
      thread turns the first of those\n from a disc read plus JSON parse into a dictionary
      hit.\n \n\nFailures are swallowed on purpose, and that is what makes this safe
      to call off the\n main thread: the warm has no synchronization context, so
      the read's continuation \u2014 the\n JsonUtility.FromJson{T}(string) of a plain
      struct \u2014 resumes on a pool thread.\n If that were ever rejected it throws
      BEFORE `cache[key]` is written while the\n `finally` still releases the per-file
      semaphore, so the awaited request every caller\n still makes redoes the work
      correctly on their own thread. Worst case is today's\n behaviour."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
