  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.Remote.BasisFaceVisibilityMirrorTests
    MemberName: BasisFaceVisibilityMirrorTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Pins the managed\u2192native face-visibility mirror that lets the gaze
      selector run without a\n per-player main-thread gather.\n\n BasisLocalEyeDriver
      used to walk BasisNetworkPlayers.ReceiversSnapshot every rescore purely\n to
      marshal one managed bool (BasisRemotePlayer.FaceIsVisible) per player into
      a NativeArray\n the Burst scorer could read. That loop is gone: the job now
      walks RemoteBoneJobSystem's dense\n SoA slots itself and reads visibility out
      of a native mirror keyed by player ID.\n\n That trades a main-thread loop for
      a sync invariant, and this file guards it. The mirror is\n keyed by player
      ID rather than SoA slot precisely so it cannot desync when RemoveRemotePlayer\n
      swap-compacts the SoA \u2014 nothing moves. What is left to protect is the
      write path itself, and\n its one ordering hazard: BasisRemotePlayer's setter
      can fire before NetworkReceiver is linked\n and has no key to write through.
      That case must fail CLOSED (leave the mirror hidden, so the\n player is skipped)
      rather than open (stale \"visible\", so the local player stares at a face\n
      that isn't rendered)."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
