    Summary: "Pins the batched gizmo backend (BasisGizmoManager): the line-mesh vertex
      layout that\n Unity actually accepts (the first in-editor run failed on attribute
      ordering \u2014 Color\n must precede TexCoords and the struct must match byte-for-byte),
      the ribbon quad\n pairing that keeps segments untwisted, the icosphere's \xD81
      parity with the built-in\n sphere the old prefab used, and the id lifecycle
      the fifteen-odd consumer systems\n rely on. Sphere/line slots are plain data
      (no scene objects), so everything here\n runs in edit mode; text gizmos create
      GameObjects and are deliberately not covered."
