  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.NamePlate.BasisNamePlateAnchorTests
    MemberName: BasisNamePlateAnchorTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Pins where a remote player's nameplate sits vertically.\n\n The placement
      used to be `hips.y + 1.2 * (liveScale / modelScale)`: a fixed 1.2 metres\n
      above the HIPS, with the only per-avatar term being a runtime-resize ratio
      that is 1.0 for\n every avatar nobody rescaled. No part of it read the avatar's
      head, so the height the plate\n actually cleared the head by was 1.2 minus
      that avatar's hips\u2192crown distance \u2014 passable on\n the ~1.75 m human
      the constant was tuned on, half a metre of empty air over a chibi, and\n NEGATIVE
      on anything tall, which renders the plate inside the avatar's chest. That is
      the\n \"some avatars are higher or lower\" report: the error is exactly each
      avatar's deviation from\n one particular body plan, so it reads as random per
      avatar rather than uniformly wrong.\n\n The replacement measures each avatar's
      own crown at registration\n (BasisNamePlateAnchorMath) and adds a proportional
      gap. These tests are written\n against a corpus of body plans rather than a
      single rig, because a single rig is precisely\n what let the old constant look
      correct for years."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
