    Summary: "Pins the nameplate overlay limiter policy (BasisNamePlateOverlayCore):
      the nearest-K\n selection that bounds how many chat bubbles / avatar-loading
      displays render at once,\n the loading-text quantization that stops far-too-frequent
      TMP re-tessellation during\n avatar downloads, and the idle-release rule that
      stops \"every player who ever chatted\n keeps a TMP forever\" accumulation.
      These rules are what keeps the overlay cost constant\n at 1000 players \u2014
      a regression here silently reverts the nameplates to unbounded cost."
