  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.UI.NamePlate.BasisNamePlateAnchorMath
    MemberName: EstimateCrownAboveRoot
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 5
    ParamNames:
    - hipsAboveRoot
    - headAboveRoot
    - eyeAboveRoot
    - boundsTopAboveRoot
    - 0f
    ParamDocs:
    - Hips bone height above the animator root at T-pose.
    - Head bone height above the animator root at T-pose.
    - "Authored centre-eye height (`BasisAvatar.AvatarEyePosition.x`);\n pass 0 or
      anything at/below the head bone to declare it absent."
    - Highest renderer bounds top above the root at T-pose.
    - False when no renderer could be measured.
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Estimates the top of the avatar's head in root-relative rendered metres.\n\n
      Two independent sources, because neither is sufficient alone: the authored
      eye height\n tells us the size of the head but not what is on top of it, and
      the renderer bounds tell\n us the whole silhouette but cannot say which part
      of it is the head. The eye-derived\n skull crown is the floor, the bounds raise
      it to real hair/hat geometry, and the cap keeps\n non-head geometry out."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
