    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The distance from the hips to the plate's BOTTOM EDGE, in rendered
      metres. The hips are\n the anchor because the hips world pose is what the network
      actually carries and what the\n placement jobs already hold; the head bone's
      world position exists per frame too, but it\n dips and bobs with head tracking,
      and a plate that bobs with the wearer's neck reads as\n broken. Measuring a
      fixed T-pose height off the hips keeps the plate steady."
