  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.UI.NamePlate.BasisRemoteNamePlateDriver
    MemberName: LocalViewerNamePlateScale
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - 0f
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Nameplates are sized in metres, so they must track the VIEWER's avatar
      size or a small avatar\n sees adult-sized plates filling its view. Was AppliedUpScale,
      which is only the explicit scale\n MODIFICATION \u2014 1.0 for a naturally-short
      avatar, so that viewer got no compensation at all \u2014\n and was additionally
      gated to scale down but never up. Now the same size ratio every other UI\n
      system uses (BasisMenuMover, BasisUIRaycast, BasisDirectTouch, BasisOnScreenControls)."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
