  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.BasisBeeFileDrop
    MemberName: BasisBeeFileDrop
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Turns a BEE file dropped onto the window into a library entry.\n\n
      A BEE is encrypted, so a path alone is not enough \u2014 the password has to
      come from\n somewhere. The SDK's bundle build already writes one next to the
      file it produced\n (`dontuploadmepassword.txt`), so a drop looks beside the
      BEE first; see\n TryFindSidecarPassword for the full search order. When that
      password opens\n the bundle and its metadata names a content type, the entry
      is added and the library\n switches to the tab it landed on.\n\n Everything
      else \u2014 no password beside the file, a password that does not open it,
      a bundle\n with no content metadata, or something already in the library \u2014
      opens the normal add\n dialog pre-filled with whatever was worked out, plus
      a line saying why. Nothing is ever\n added on a guess: an entry the user did
      not confirm would sit in their library failing to\n load with no obvious cause."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
