  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.BasisContentNameVersion
    MemberName: BasisContentNameVersion
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Reads a version out of a content NAME, for library entries that have
      no\n BasisBundleDescription.ContentGroupId to group by.\n\n \n\nContentGroupId
      is authored in the SDK, so nothing built before it exists carries one \u2014\n
      and that is precisely the content a creator has been re-uploading by hand under
      names like\n \"My Avatar v2\". Falling back to the name lets those stack into
      one card the same way a\n grouped upload does, instead of scattering across
      the library as unrelated entries.\n\n\n\nThis is a heuristic over creator-chosen
      text, so it is deliberately conservative: it\n only ever strips a version-looking
      token from the END of a name, and never strips one when\n doing so would leave
      nothing but punctuation and digits behind."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.BasisContentNameVersion
    MemberName: StripVersionSuffix
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(name)
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "A trailing version token in any of the spellings creators actually
      use:\n \"(2)\", \"[v3]\", \" v1.4\", \"_V2\", \" - 3\", \"5\". Alternatives
      share the `num` group,\n which .NET allows, so the numeric part is read back
      the same way whichever matched."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
