  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.SettingsProvider
    MemberName: SettingsProvider
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 1
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Search across the whole Settings menu, driven from the panel header's
      Search button rather\n than a field on every page. The popup owns the typing
      and the result list; this side owns the\n index \u2014 every tab is walked
      for matches, including the ones the user never opened, so a\n setting can be
      found from wherever they happen to be.\n\n \n\nBuilding the tabs nobody has
      opened \u2014 and expanding their lazy sections so their rows\n exist to be
      found \u2014 instantiates a page worth of prefabs each, so it runs one page
      per frame\n in the background and tells the popup to ask again as each one
      lands."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
