  - TypeFullName: 
    MemberName: UpdatePlayerControlForRole
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - 0
    ParamDocs:
    - The role whose actions will be executed.
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Dispatches a role's actions once per frame using the combined input
      state of every device\n currently holding that role. This makes edge-triggered
      actions (menu toggle, mic, jump) fire\n exactly once per role even when two
      devices share a hand role \u2014 e.g. a duplicate controller\n left over from
      a SteamVR reconnect, or hand-tracking coexisting with a controller. Booleans\n
      are OR'd across holders so either one can trigger an edge (see BasisInputState.MergeFrom).\n
      With a single holder (the common case) the aggregate equals that device, so
      behaviour is\n unchanged. Used for roles that may legitimately have multiple
      holders; other roles dispatch\n directly through UpdatePlayerControl."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
