  - TypeFullName: 
    MemberName: DeviceScale
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The wrist the avatar's hand bone is actually driven to, expressed in
      the same unscaled player\n space as BasisInput.UnscaledDeviceCoord.\n\n Every
      backend builds HandFinal as OffsetCoords \u2297 (wrist \xD7 DeviceScale), so
      undoing\n that recovers the wrist wherever the backend's raw pose happens to
      sit. OpenVR already bakes the\n wrist into the device coord, so this lands
      back on the same point and nothing changes; OpenXR\n leaves the device coord
      on the grip pose while the bone goes to the palm minus a wrist offset, so\n
      there the two differ by several cm per hand.\n\n Arm-span calibration has to
      sample this rather than the raw device pose: measuring a landmark the\n hand
      bone never occupies makes the player look longer-armed than they are, and the
      body fit spends\n the whole difference stretching the avatar's arms."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
