  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Device_Management.Devices.Pairing.BasisVirtualMidpointInput
    MemberName: BasisVirtualMidpointInput
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: BasisInput
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Virtual BasisInput created by the pairing service when the user\n links
      two physical trackers together. Each frame it polls both partners,\n produces
      a single midpoint pose, and publishes that pose as if it were a\n real device.
      Calibration sees only this virtual sample for the pair (the\n physical bases
      are skipped via BasisInput.IsLinked), so a\n linked pair claims one body role
      together.\n\n The fusion is a continuous confidence-weighted blend rather than
      a hard\n \"trust one, drop the other\" choice. Each tracker carries a per-frame\n
      confidence derived from how surprising its current motion is relative to\n
      its recent baseline (a sudden velocity spike \u2014 typical of an occluded
      or\n glitching tracker \u2014 collapses its weight; smooth motion keeps it
      near 1).\n On top of that, both halves are softly pulled toward the calibrated
      rest\n distance whenever they drift apart, with strength that ramps continuously\n
      with the divergence so small flex/slop barely shifts anything but a real\n
      divergence is partly absorbed. Both sources always contribute, which gives\n
      the noise-averaging benefit of two measurements while still degrading\n gracefully
      when one half misbehaves."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
