  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.Calibration.
    MemberName: WithoutEyeHeightCompensation_ADrag_LosesTheLegsAndHips
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - Body.Standard(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "If the eye-height capture ever stops subtracting the play-space offset,
      the floor lands at the\n dragged height while the priors stay eye-relative,
      and legs/hips stop classifying. This is the\n paired negative that keeps the
      invariance gate above honest."
    Remarks: 
