  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.Calibration.
    MemberName: TrackedFloor_CancelsAnyVerticalShift_EvenOnesBasisCannotSee
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - Body.Standard(
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "\"Calibrate anywhere\": with body trackers present, the floor comes
      from the trackers\n themselves (BasisCalibrationMath.TryEstimateFloorFromTrackers),
      so the eye height \u2014 and with\n it the whole classification frame \u2014
      cancels ANY vertical shift, including ones Basis has no\n bookkeeping for (an
      OVRAS/SteamVR space drag, a stale grounding lift). This sweeps shifts\n with
      NO compensation term at all and requires identical eye height and identical
      roles."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
