  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.Sync.BasisFingerBlockCodecTests
    MemberName: BasisFingerBlockCodecTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Round-trip and robustness of the curl/splay scalar codec that replaced
      the finger rotations.\n\n Fidelity is asserted in DEGREES AT THE JOINT rather
      than in wire units, because wire units\n are meaningless on their own: curl
      spans roughly 100\xB0 of flexion and splay roughly 50\xB0 of\n abduction, so
      the same quantiser step buys very different accuracy on each. Asserting the\n
      angle is what makes a future bit-budget change show up as a fidelity number
      instead of a\n silently-passing test.\n\n The clamp and NaN cases are not hypothetical.
      MediaPipe applies CurlGain/SplayGain to an\n angle ratio and can exceed 1,
      and a dropped tracking frame can hand through a NaN \u2014 an\n unguarded cast
      of either into an unsigned quantiser is how a hand ends up locked in a fist."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
