  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.Sync.BasisFingerCrossRigTests
    MemberName: BasisFingerCrossRigTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The claim v47 rests on, tested against real humanoid rigs: nothing
      about finger geometry\n crosses the wire, so a hand pose authored by one player
      has to come out PROPORTIONALLY right\n on whatever avatar the viewer happens
      to be drawing.\n\n The mechanism is that curl/splay are muscle-space quantities
      and each receiver expands them\n through a grid baked from its own rig. If
      that holds, two rigs whose fingers differ in length\n by 60% still produce
      the same joint angles and the same extension fraction for the same wire\n values
      \u2014 and, crucially, an avatar scaled 2x produces bit-identical grid cells,
      because\n rotations do not scale.\n\n These use procedurally built humanoids
      (BasisHumanoidRigFixture) rather than a project asset\n so the finger proportions
      can be dialled deliberately instead of being whatever some test\n avatar happened
      to ship with."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
