  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.Sync.
    MemberName: SweepingCurl_OpensMonotonically
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - Bake(rig
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Curl has to move the hand in one direction across its whole range.
      A grid that folded back\n on itself would read as a finger that opens, closes
      slightly, then opens again: an\n artefact only visible while someone slowly
      releases a trigger.\n\n Curl runs CURLED -> OPEN, so extension rises. An earlier
      version asserted the opposite\n direction with a 0.02 tolerance, which exceeded
      the real per-step change (~0.006 over 40\n steps) and so could never fail -
      it passed while claiming the reverse of what it measured.\n The travel assertion
      at the end is what stops that from recurring silently."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
