  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.Sync.BasisFingerWireSizeTests
    MemberName: BasisFingerWireSizeTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Pins the exact geometry of the rotation bitstream.\n\n Every number
      here was recomputed from the tables rather than copied from a comment, because\n
      the comments had already drifted once: BPC_HIGH claimed 1182 bits / 148 rotation
      bytes / a\n 169-byte packet against a then-real 1302 / 163 / 232, and all four
      tiers understated the\n packet by the hips-rotation tail.\n\n v47 split the
      region in two. Slots 0..20 still carry smallest-three rotations; the thirty\n
      finger joints that used to follow them are gone, replaced by ten curl/splay
      channels. The\n share those fingers used to cost \u2014 41.9% of the High stream
      \u2014 is the budget this was measured\n against, so the before/after figures
      are asserted rather than described."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
