  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.Sync.BasisGenericBoneRotationTests
    MemberName: BasisGenericBoneRotationTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Locks the RIG-NEUTRAL bone rotation space the avatar stream carries\n
      (BasisGenericBoneRotation).\n\n The stream used to carry each bone's T-pose-relative
      LOCAL delta, which is expressed in\n whatever local axes the modeller authored
      that bone with. One rig runs +X down the forearm,\n the next runs +Y down it:
      the same visible elbow bend is a different number on each, so the\n pose could
      only ever be replayed on the exact avatar that produced it. What goes on the\n
      wire now is the joint's rotation away from its own rest pose expressed in the
      CHARACTER's\n axes, which any rig can read using only its own rest data.\n\n
      What these guard, in order of how load-bearing they are:\n   - the wire value
      is literally the character-space rotation (the definition holds),\n   - a pose
      encoded on one rig replays correctly on a completely different rig,\n   - the
      OLD scheme fails that same test, so the change is doing real work,\n   - the
      remap is LOSSLESS: cross-rig error through the real codec equals the same-rig\n    
      quantiser error that was already there, which is what lets the bit budget,
      the\n     MAX_COMPONENT ranges and the packet size all stay exactly as they
      were,\n   - an identity rest frame reproduces the legacy scheme bit for bit,
      which is the\n     degradation path for a bone a rig does not have,\n   - the
      shared pure-C# math agrees with Unity.Mathematics, since the Burst jobs on
      both\n     ends use math.mul while the server and these tests use the portable
      implementation."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
