  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.Sync.
    MemberName: ThroughRealCodec_CrossRigErrorIsExactlyTheQuantiserError
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - frameA
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "End to end through the REAL smallest-three codec at High quality, per
      bone slot, with\n its real per-slot bit count and component range.\n\n The
      assertion is deliberately not \"cross-rig error is small\" \u2014 it is that
      the cross-rig\n error EQUALS the error a same-rig stream already suffers from
      quantisation alone. That\n is the precise claim: the remap contributes nothing,
      so the coarsest slots are no worse\n off than they were before the change."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
