  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.Sync.
    MemberName: RigsWithDifferentRootFacing_StillTransfer
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "The bug this basis exists to fix, reproduced end to end.\n\n TposeFromRoot
      divides out where the avatar is STANDING, but not the rotation an\n exporter
      baked between the animator transform and the skeleton \u2014 a Blender Z-up\n
      conversion node, an `Armature` child rotated \u221290\xB0 about X, a model
      authored facing \u2212Z.\n All are legal humanoid rigs (Unity's Avatar constrains
      the rig definition, not the\n GameObject hierarchy above it) and each puts
      a different constant inside F.\n\n That constant cancels whenever both ends
      wear the same rig, which is why it stayed\n hidden: the ONLY time a pose is
      decoded on a foreign rig is the avatar-swap window,\n where the old avatar
      stays worn while the new one downloads and the far end is already\n streaming
      the new one. Reported as limbs twisting AND the whole avatar offsetting for
      a\n few frames, then snapping correct once the new avatar landed.\n\n Here
      rig B's root is turned 90\xB0 about Y relative to rig A's \u2014 the same character,\n
      exported facing a different way. Without the basis normalisation the retarget
      is wrong\n by that 90\xB0; with it, the two agree."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
