  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.Sync.BasisHumanoidRigFixture
    MemberName: BasisHumanoidRigFixture
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: System.IDisposable
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Builds throwaway humanoid rigs in memory so finger tests can run against
      real\n HumanPoseHandler muscle space without depending on any avatar asset.\n\n
      The point of having two of them is the claim the finger block rests on: nothing
      about finger\n geometry crosses the wire, so a pose authored on one rig has
      to reproduce PROPORTIONALLY on a\n rig with different finger lengths. That
      is only testable with two rigs whose hands genuinely\n differ, which is what
      FingerScale and HandScale are for.\n\n Bones are authored directly in T-pose
      (arms down \xB1X, legs down \u2212Y) because that is the pose\n Unity's humanoid
      retarget is defined against and the pose the grid bake samples from."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
