    Summary: "The canonical-hand-frame grip path, driven owner-to-observer the way
      two clients actually work:\n the real OnBeforeTransmit measures on one rig
      and the real receive path decodes on a SEPARATE rig\n with its OWN bone layout.\n\n
      BasisPickupWristFrameTests covers the legacy wrist-bone encoding, which only
      reconstructs when both\n ends have the same avatar. These give the two ends
      genuinely different rigs \u2014 different wrist bind\n rotations, different
      hand sizes, and in one case no fingers at all \u2014 because that is the case
      the\n frame exists for: an observer drawing a fallback or substitute avatar
      must still get the prop into\n the hand it is drawing."
