  - TypeFullName: Basis.Tests.Sync.BasisPickupWeldFixture
    MemberName: BasisPickupWeldFixture
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 1
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Two clients of one held prop, wired the way production wires them:
      the holder resolves its hand\n frame through the LOCAL branch of BasisHandGrip.TryGetPlayerFrame
      (the local rig\n driver's mapping) and the observer through the REMOTE branch
      (that remote's avatar driver\n references), each with its own rig in its own
      place.\n\n That split is the whole point. The reconstruction is a change of
      coordinates, so it is exact for\n ANY frame as long as both ends build the
      same one \u2014 which means a networked hold can only be wrong\n if the two
      ends disagree, and the two ends can only disagree where they resolve differently.
      Suites\n that make both ends a BasisRemotePlayer exercise one branch twice
      and cannot see it.\n\n The real transmit (`OnBeforeTransmit`) and the real
      receive path (driver schedule \u2192 complete \u2192\n reweld) run; only the
      input stack and the transport are staged."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
