    Summary: "Direct unit coverage for the configurable jitter-buffer depth on BasisSyncReceiver\n
      (the `bufferDepth` argument to BasisSyncReceiver.Configure). The latency harness\n
      exercises this end-to-end; these pin the receiver mechanism itself: the floor
      is seeded and clamped,\n the default argument preserves the historical depth-2
      behaviour byte-for-byte, a lower floor settles\n to a shallower steady buffer
      (the latency win), and the depth still adapts upward under starvation."
