  - TypeFullName: BasisVisemeContextLifecycleTests
    MemberName: BasisVisemeContextLifecycleTests
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "A remote's OpenLipSync context is pooled: it is disposed once they
      go quiet or leave viseme\n range, and a brand new instance is allocated when
      they speak again. Anything reading\n openLipSyncContext has to re-read it every
      tick \u2014 the HVR comms bridge cached it and its\n LastApplied array instead,
      which froze remote Voice Gain and visemes at 0 after the speaker's\n first
      pause. These lock the release side of that contract; HVRBuiltInAddressPublisherTests\n
      locks the reader side."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
