  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.BasisAudioRangeSliderLimit
    MemberName: BasisAudioRangeSliderLimit
    Kind: Enum
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: MonoBehaviour
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Pins the local Microphone/Hearing Range slider's upper bound to the
      ceiling the server\n pushes. Settings pages are built once per menu open and
      read the ceiling as they build, so\n an admin raising or lowering the limit
      would otherwise leave every panel that is already up\n showing the maximum
      it was built with \u2014 including the admin's own, since the server echoes\n
      the change back to the client that sent it.\n \n\n\n Lives on the slider's
      own GameObject so it dies with it, and re-reads on enable as well as\n on the
      event, which covers a section that was collapsed (and so disabled) while the
      limit\n moved. The effective range is capped separately by\n SMModuleDistanceBasedReductions.SetMicrophoneRangeCapMeters
      /\n SMModuleDistanceBasedReductions.SetHearingRangeCapMeters; this is only
      the UI\n catching up with it."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
