  - TypeFullName: Basis.BasisUI.LibraryProviderDialogCheckForUpdate
    MemberName: LibraryProviderDialogCheckForUpdate
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "User-driven cache invalidation for content published to a STATIC url.\n\n
      \n\nCache identity is the url, so re-uploading a bee to the same address is
      invisible to a\n client that already has it \u2014 the load path never touches
      the network again. This asks the\n host whether the bytes changed (one small
      conditional request, no payload), and on a change\n evicts the cached copy
      so the next load fetches fresh.\n\n\n\nOnly the person who published the content
      knows they changed it, which is why this is\n a button rather than something
      automatic: the check is cheap but not free, and doing it on\n every load would
      add a round trip to every avatar in the instance."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
