  - TypeFullName: Basis.IK.Debugging.BasisIKSweepBatch
    MemberName: BasisIKSweepBatch
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Headless entry points for the IK sweeps, so a gate can be checked without
      opening an editor\n window. The sweeps themselves are unchanged -- this only
      drives them.\n\n Why: BasisIKTestGates carries pass/fail thresholds that are
      only reachable through\n the IK Sweeps window (Elbow Protect / Run All), i.e.
      by hand. That means the numbers\n they encode drift out of date silently. ElbowMinClearedFraction
      is the worked example -- its\n comment claims a ~0.64 ceiling that was measured
      before several collider and arm-solve changes.\n\n   Unity.exe -runTests is
      for the NUnit suite; this is for the sweeps:\n   Unity.exe -batchmode -quit
      -projectPath <p> -executeMethod Basis.IK.Debugging.BasisIKSweepBatch.ElbowProtect"
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
