  - TypeFullName: 
    MemberName: SetGizmoLayer
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 2
    ParamNames:
    - linkedID
    - BasisDebug.LogTag.Gizmo
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Puts one gizmo on a specific Unity layer instead of the shared RenderLayer,\n
      so a camera that culls that layer cannot see it. Pass -1 to hand it back to
      RenderLayer.\n \n\n\n The layer is the only thing that hides a gizmo from a
      particular camera. Draws are\n submitted for every camera in the frame, and
      the batch is built from wherever the\n producer last left it \u2014 Render
      runs at the tail of LateUpdate, so a\n producer that writes its positions later
      (in the before-render pass, as the player\n rig and anything parented to it
      do) is a frame ahead of the geometry being drawn.\n Parking geometry outside
      a camera's frustum is therefore not a guarantee: the shot is\n taken from this
      frame's pose while the gizmo still sits at the last one. The handheld\n camera's
      detached wireframe marker uses this to stay out of its own capture.\n \n\n\n\n\n
      Text labels are GameObjects rather than batched draws, so for those this writes
      the\n object's layer there and then \u2014 including the -1 case, which resolves
      to the current\n RenderLayer rather than tracking later changes to it."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
