  - TypeFullName: Basis.MediaPipe.MediaPipeArmConverter
    MemberName: MediaPipeArmConverter
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Retargets the arms from PoseLandmarker WORLD landmarks (metric metres,
      real depth) instead of\n image positions.\n\n Wrist and elbow are measured
      relative to the user's own shoulder, expressed in a body frame built\n from
      their shoulder line and torso, then divided by the user's own arm length. What
      is left is a\n unitless \"fraction of my reach, in my body's frame\" vector
      that does not care how far from the\n camera the user sits or how long their
      arms are. Multiplying by the avatar's arm length and\n applying the avatar's
      body frame \u2014 built by the exact same rule \u2014 puts the hand where it
      is on you.\n\n Reach matching alone still misses when the avatar's head sits
      at a different height above the\n shoulders than yours, which is precisely
      the \"hand next to my face\" case, so the vertical component\n is blended toward
      a head-relative scale as the hand rises to head height."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
