  - TypeFullName: Basis.MediaPipe.MediaPipeHandConverter
    MemberName: MediaPipeHandConverter
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "MediaPipe 21-point hand landmarks \u2192 finger curl/splay (BasisLocalHandDriver)
      plus the wrist\n rotation for the hand trackers. Both run off the metric WORLD
      landmarks, so curl no longer\n collapses when the hand points at the camera
      and the palm frame is real 3D rather than a\n projection.\n\n Rotation is a
      retarget, not a calibration: the palm frame is measured relative to the user's
      torso\n and re-expressed relative to the avatar's, then corrected by the constant
      that maps a palm frame\n onto the avatar's hand bone. Holding your hand however
      you like reproduces it on the avatar with\n nothing to calibrate."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
