    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Why the hand's side may not be guessed from a label. Chirality is baked
      into the palm frame \u2014 the\n normal is negated for a left hand \u2014 so
      reading a hand as the wrong side returns a frame rolled 180\n degrees about
      the forearm. The position still lands correctly, which is what makes it present
      as\n \"the arms work but the wrists are wrong\"."
