    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "True if the player can open `url` directly, without a resolver:\n any
      non-HTTP scheme (transport like rtsp/rtmp/rist, or a local file), or an\n http(s)
      URL whose path ends in a media-container extension\n (.mp4/.m4v/.m4a/.m4s/.ts/.m2ts/.mts/.m3u8/.wav/.webm/.opus/.mp3).
      An http(s) URL with no media extension is a page URL\n (e.g. a YouTube/Twitch
      watch page) and needs a resolver. This is the single\n source of truth for
      the live-vs-resolve steering; resolvers and callers both\n consult it. It classifies
      only \u2014 it never blocks (host trust is separate)."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
