  - TypeFullName: OpenLipSync.Inference.VisemeSmoother
    MemberName: VisemeSmoother
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Temporal smoother for viseme probabilities that does not push the mouth
      late.\n\n \n\nThe plain one-pole this replaces \u2014 `y[n] = a*y[n-1] + (1-a)*x[n]`
      \u2014 is a lag\n network. Its group delay is `a/(1-a)` frames, so the shipped
      default of a = 0.7 at\n the model's fixed 100 Hz hop held every viseme 23 ms
      behind the audio, purely to\n reject frame-to-frame jitter. That delay is spent
      before the pipeline has even handed the\n weights to the avatar, and it is
      the single largest avoidable term in the lip-sync\n latency budget.\n\n\n\nRunning
      the pole twice and extrapolating along the difference \u2014 `2*y1 - y2`,\n
      the standard double-EMA \u2014 cancels that delay exactly for a ramp input
      while keeping most\n of the noise rejection. At a = 0.7 the residual noise
      is 0.62x the raw signal against\n 0.42x for the plain pole: slightly less smoothing,
      23 ms less lag. The trade is worth\n taking because the model already spends
      20 ms of unavoidable lookahead, and lag is what\n reads as \"wrong\" on a face.\n\n\n\nCost
      is one extra multiply-add per viseme per hop \u2014 15 floats at 100 Hz per\n
      speaker, which is nothing next to the inference that produced them."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
