  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Device_Management.Devices.OpenVR.
    MemberName: WaitingUntilReady
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Pulls SteamVR's grown recommended render target (which factors in the
      lens\n distortion overlap between eyes) and bakes it into XRSettings.eyeTextureResolutionScale.\n
      The OpenVR XR plugin allocates eye textures at Unity's default size \u2014
      without this,\n Steam super-sampling and the per-headset native resolution
      are silently ignored.\n The recommendation is re-read from the runtime rather
      than taken from\n SteamVR.sceneWidth/sceneHeight, which are frozen in the SteamVR
      constructor, so\n compositor-side changes (per-app resolution, supersample
      slider, external tools\n such as OVR Dynamic Resolution) are followed while
      the client is running."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.Device_Management.Devices.OpenVR.
    MemberName: ThreadedInputUpdate
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "When true the SteamVR action-state update (UpdateActionState + button/axis/skeleton\n
      reads \u2014 the bulk of the per-frame input cost) runs on a worker thread,
      kicked from\n SimulateKick and joined in Simulate so it overlaps the\n comms/network-apply
      work between the two. OpenVR interfaces are thread-safe, the\n update path
      reads main-thread state only via SteamVR_Input.CaptureMainThreadState,\n and
      no Basis code touches action state between kick and join (readers are the eye\n
      driver before the kick, and device polls after the join)."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
