  - TypeFullName: BasisGenericBlendshapeSidecar
    MemberName: BasisGenericBlendshapeSidecar
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Blendshape payload for the Generic (glTF) avatar section. glTFast's
      exporter writes no\n morph targets, so the GLB alone loses every blendshape;
      this sidecar carries the shapes the\n avatar actually actuates (visemes, blink,
      laughter) as sparse deltas and is appended after\n the GLB inside the encrypted
      section \u2014 the GLB itself stays a pristine, standard file. On\n import
      the shapes are rebuilt onto the (still readable) glTFast meshes with\n `Mesh.AddBlendShapeFrame`
      at frame weight 100, so Basis drivers write 0..100 weights\n exactly like they
      do on AssetBundle avatars. Deltas are stored pre-scaled to full\n application
      at weight 100, which flattens multi-frame source shapes to their final frame.\n\n
      The payload arrives over the network, so parsing is defensive: hard caps on
      every count and\n any violation aborts the parse \u2014 a bad sidecar costs
      the shapes, never the avatar."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
