  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.BasisSdk.
    MemberName: IsUnset
    Kind: Property
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "True only for the entirely-zero entry a deserializer hands back for
      a table that was\n allocated but never authored.\n \n\nDeliberately strict
      rather than \"cannot move its shape\". Zeroing\n Gain or collapsing the output
      range is exactly how a creator switches a\n viseme OFF, and that intent has
      to survive \u2014 rebuilding those on the default hands the\n shape back to
      the model, which parks the mouth open on whatever the model reports at\n rest.
      A profile with nothing set at all is the only unambiguous \"absent\"."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.BasisSdk.BasisVisemeDriveConfig
    MemberName: BasisVisemeDriveConfig
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Avatar-wide lip-sync response settings.\n \n\nEvery field's \"absent\"
      value is also a legal authored value \u2014 most dangerously\n BackendSmoothing,
      where 0 means \"no smoothing whatsoever\" \u2014 so an instance\n that reaches
      the runtime without its field initialisers having run is indistinguishable\n
      from a deliberate request for silence. Consumers must test IsUnset before\n
      honouring a config rather than assuming the initialisers below always apply."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
