  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.BasisSdk.Constraints.BasisConstraintBase
    MemberName: BasisConstraintBase
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: MonoBehaviour
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 1
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Shared authoring surface for the Basis constraint components \u2014
      the drop-in replacement for\n Unity's built-in `UnityEngine.Animations` constraints
      (`PositionConstraint`,\n `RotationConstraint`, and friends). The public shape
      deliberately mirrors Unity's\n `IConstraint` (weight, constraintActive, locked,\n
      `AddSource` / `GetSource` / `SetSource` / `RemoveSource`) so porting a rig\n
      is a component swap rather than a rewrite.\n\n Data-only, exactly like BasisAuthoredMotion:
      there is no per-instance\n `Update`. Every enabled component is folded into
      one batched, Burst-compiled solve in\n the framework-side `BasisConstraintSystem`,
      which is why this type lives in the SDK\n assembly and speaks only plain Unity
      types \u2014 the SDK cannot see the framework.\n\n The framework subscribes
      to ActiveStateChanged and StructureChanged\n once at startup; components announce
      themselves across the assembly boundary through those\n statics rather than
      holding a reference to any system.\n\n Scalar state (weight, offsets, masks,
      at-rest pose) is re-read from the component every frame,\n so tweaking it live
      \u2014 in the inspector or from script \u2014 just works. Changing the *shape*
      of\n sources is a structural edit: go through the source API below, or call\n
      SetDirty if you mutate the serialized list directly."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
