  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.BasisSdk.Constraints.BasisParentConstraint
    MemberName: BasisParentConstraint
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: BasisConstraintBase
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Drives a transform's local position and rotation together, as if it
      were parented to the\n weighted average of its sources. The Basis stand-in
      for\n `UnityEngine.Animations.ParentConstraint`.\n\n Each source carries its
      own position/rotation offset, so a single constrained transform can\n sit at
      a different relative pose per source \u2014 that is what makes a two-source
      parent\n constraint blend smoothly between, say, a hip holster and a hand.\n\n
      Not to be confused with `Basis.Scripts.BasisSdk.Interactions.BasisParentConstraint`,\n
      the serialized helper class the pickup and held-camera interactables evaluate
      inline. This\n is the scene-authorable component; that one is an internal building
      block."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
