  - TypeFullName: BasisGraphicsStatePrewarm
    MemberName: BasisGraphicsStatePrewarm
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Record-then-replay PSO cache layered on top of BasisShaderPrewarm.\n
      ShaderVariantCollection.WarmUp only compiles the shader variant; on the explicit-pipeline\n
      backends (D3D12 / Vulkan / Metal) the first-draw hitch is the full Pipeline
      State Object \u2014\n variant + vertex layout + blend/depth/stencil + render-target
      formats \u2014 which the legacy\n path can't know ahead of time. GraphicsStateCollection
      traces the real PSOs that render and\n persists them, so a later session can
      pre-create them.\n\n This is complementary, not a replacement: BasisShaderPrewarm
      stays the proactive first-load\n warm for never-before-seen content; this drains
      a chunk of last session's traced PSOs at each\n content-load point, where the
      matching shaders are now resident. The reliable win is the base\n app plus
      any content the player re-loads across sessions.\n\n Two instances of the same
      file are kept because Unity forbids warming a collection that is\n actively
      tracing: _warm is loaded read-only and warmed at content loads, while\n _trace
      is loaded and traced all session, then evicted-to-cap and saved at flush.\n\n
      Growth is bounded by a hard variant cap with best-effort eviction at flush.
      True per-variant LRU\n isn't possible here: the API exposes no usage timestamp,
      warming pre-creates a PSO so the trace\n never re-observes its reuse, and a
      variant whose shader has unloaded has no stable identity to\n track. Eviction
      drops not-currently-resident variants first, then the most recently traced\n
      (protecting the long-lived base-app set). The cap alone guarantees the file
      can't grow without limit."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
