    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Measures the avatar's own lighting clamps the same shader-agnostic
      way the matte works:\n render under black, reference-white and 2x-overbright
      ambient into an HDR target and\n compare per-pixel luminance. Toon shaders
      floor their light term (avatars never go\n fully dark) and cap it (never blow
      out) \u2014 matching that at runtime is what keeps the\n far avatar from standing
      out in dark or bright worlds. Median ratios so emissive\n patches and rim tricks
      don't skew the estimate."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
