  - TypeFullName: BasisIconCapture
    MemberName: BasisIconCapture
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Renders an icon for a piece of Basis content and writes it into the
      project as a PNG.\n\n \n\nTwo capture paths, because the three content types
      want different framing: models\n (props, avatars) render isolated in a preview
      scene so nothing around them ends up in the\n shot, while a whole scene can
      only be photographed through a camera that is actually in it.\n\n\n\nThe result
      is written to disk as a real texture asset rather than kept in memory, so the\n
      icon survives domain reloads and can be reassigned by hand later. Assignment
      goes through the\n content's SerializedObject so Ctrl+Z restores the previous
      icon \u2014 the PNG itself\n stays on disk, the same way undoing any \"create
      asset\" button in Unity leaves the file behind."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
