  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.Core.BasisCpuBudget
    MemberName: ConcurrencyWidth
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 3
    ParamNames:
    - 2
    - 16
    - max
    ParamDocs:
    - Stripes wanted per core.
    - Floor, so a single-core host still gets a usable table.
    - Ceiling, so a very large host does not allocate an absurd table.
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Sizes a per-thread-contention structure \u2014 stripe tables, shard
      counts, pools whose only\n job is to keep concurrent threads off each other's
      cache lines.\n\n Always derived, never a literal. Hosts this runs on range
      from a couple of container\n vCPUs to hundreds of cores, and a constant picked
      on one of them is wrong everywhere\n else in a way that never shows up as an
      error \u2014 just contention nobody attributes. The\n result is rounded up
      to a power of two so callers can index it with a mask."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
