  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.Core.
    MemberName: System.Math.Min
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 2
    ParamNames:
    - 4
    - floor
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Ceiling on runtime-added send sockets when the operator has not set
      one.\n\n Half the cores. A socket is not free \u2014 it is a receive thread
      that spends its life in a\n syscall, so the ceiling has to leave room for the
      pools that do the actual work; and it\n is not expensive either, which is why
      the answer is a share of the machine rather than a\n number. Field measurement
      on a 128-core host with weak cores found real gains all the\n way up to 64
      sockets, which is what this returns there. Growth still has to earn each\n
      one against the drop counter; this only bounds how far that can go.\n\n Floored
      at four so a small host can still spread across a few flows, but never above
      the\n core count \u2014 on a 2-core container, four receive threads is the
      whole machine spinning\n in recvfrom."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
