  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.Core.BasisNetworkCommons
    MemberName: MinimumPeerMtu
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 1
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Largest payload a caller may hand to a send that the transport cannot
      fragment\n (see CanFragment). Over this, the send THROWS rather than truncating
      or\n dropping, so anything sizing a packet has to check first.\n\n Deliberately
      derived from the smallest MTU any peer can be at, not the negotiated one.\n
      A peer starts at its initial MTU and only grows through discovery, and one
      broadcast\n fans out to peers at different points in that \u2014 including
      P2P links that negotiated\n separately from the server link. Sizing against
      a live `peer.Mtu` would produce a\n payload that fits the peer it was measured
      on and throws on the one still probing.\n The slack absorbs the packet header
      plus any per-message framing above it."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
