  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.Core.
    MemberName: CompressedAvatarBundleChannel
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 1
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Server-only outbound channel carrying multiple avatar quality messages\n
      to a single receiver, LZ4-compressed into one UDP datagram that fits the peer
      MTU.\n Wire format (v50):\n   [count:1][rawLen:2-LE][LZ4 block( group* )]\n  
      group := [origChannel:1][n:1][msgLen:2-LE] x n [bodies]\n Each [origChannel]
      is the byte-id or ushort-id avatar quality channel the message would\n have
      been sent on individually (channels 6-13 / 41-48), or DeltaAvatarChannel. One\n
      channel byte per RUN, not per entry \u2014 the server channel-sorts a receiver's
      pending\n messages first so the runs are long, but decoding does not depend
      on that.\n The DeltaAvatarChannel group's bodies are COLUMN-TRANSPOSED (byte
      j of every body, then\n byte j+1 of every body); no other group is. See BasisAvatarBundleCodec,
      which is the\n shared reader, and BundleCompressionExperiment for why.\n Compression:
      LZ4Codec.Encode at LZ4Level.L00_FAST (K4os.Compression.LZ4 1.3.x)."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
