  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.Core.BasisP2PLinkHealth
    MemberName: BasisP2PLinkHealth
    Kind: Enum
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Pure decision logic for BasisP2PManager's direct-link (P2P) health
      watchdog \u2014 the part that\n decides when a Connected direct link has gone
      dead / one-way and must fall back to the server\n relay so voice and avatar
      don't freeze. Extracted from the client (which is Unity-only and can't\n be
      unit-tested headless) so the thresholds and their ordering can be pinned by
      tests.\n\n This is the mechanism that makes a direct-connected pair recover
      after one of them rejoins:\n the rejoiner's old socket goes silent, no inbound
      P2P arrives, and the link is demoted back to\n the server relay. If this logic
      (or the timer that drives it) is wrong, the pair stays routed\n over a dead
      direct link and can't hear each other \u2014 the reported symptom."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
