  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.Core.
    MemberName: SliceCap
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 2
    ParamNames:
    - configured
    - 1
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Upper bound on reduction-system slicing.\n\n Slicing is the last-resort
      lever: it divides the roster so each tick serves only part of\n it. The cap
      decides how far the server may degrade before it simply overruns instead,\n
      and 32 was chosen when 2000 was a large instance. At 8000 a cap of 32 still
      leaves 250\n receivers per tick, so the server hits the ceiling with nowhere
      left to go. Scaling the\n cap keeps \"degrade further\" available as an alternative
      to \"miss the tick\"."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
