  - TypeFullName: Configuration
    MemberName: BSRMaxDegreeOfParallelism
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Worker cap for the BSR tick's parallel phases (send loop, message processing,
      distance\n sweep). 0 = auto (a quarter of the cores, floored at 4 and capped
      at 8).\n\n More workers is not free: the tick runs ~275x/s, so each phase pays
      dispatch and wake cost\n per tick per worker, and every extra thread adds GC
      poll-point traffic. Measured at 500\n players on a 32-thread box: 32 workers
      = 11.0 cores, 16 = 8.6, 8 = 6.6, 4 = 6.4, at equal\n or better throughput.
      Raise it if you run far more players per instance than that and the\n profile
      shows the send loop itself saturating."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Configuration
    MemberName: BSRMaxSliceCount
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Furthest the reduction system may slice its roster under load. 0 =
      scale with population.\n\n Slicing is the last-resort lever: at slice N each
      tick serves only 1/N of the receivers, so\n everyone's update rate drops uniformly.
      The cap decides how far the server is allowed to\n degrade before it stops
      degrading and simply overruns its tick instead.\n\n It was a fixed 32, chosen
      when 2000 was a large instance. At 8000 players a cap of 32 still\n leaves
      250 receivers per tick, so a struggling server reaches the ceiling with nowhere
      left\n to go and starts missing the period \u2014 which is the failure slicing
      exists to prevent.\n Automatic holds the per-tick fan-out roughly flat as population
      grows.\n\n Set a positive value only to pin it; higher caps trade update rate
      for keeping the tick."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
