  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.Core.IBasisTransportConfigMigration
    MemberName: IBasisTransportConfigMigration
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Implemented by a transport config that needs to change values it has
      already written to\n disc, not merely gain new ones.\n\n The normal upgrade
      path deliberately preserves every value already in the file \u2014 an operator\n
      who set something meant it. That is the wrong behaviour exactly once: when
      a shipped default\n turns out to be harmful, every existing install is carrying
      it explicitly and would never\n receive the fix. A migration may then replace
      that specific value, and must leave anything\n else alone."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
