  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.Core.
    MemberName: PeerUpdatePeersPerWorker
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Peers each worker in the transport's per-peer pass is expected to service.
      Lower means\n more workers for the same population. 0 = 128.\n\n This is what
      decides how much of a large host the server can use. 128 was fitted to a\n
      32-thread machine with fast cores, and it caps workers by population rather
      than by the\n machine: at 4000 peers it picks 31 workers however many cores
      exist, so a 128-core host\n sits near a quarter utilisation. Halve it to double
      the workers.\n\n Tune against the pass time in the [CPU] log line \u2014 over
      25 ms with cores to spare means\n this is too high. Slower cores want a lower
      value, since a worker covers fewer peers."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
