  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.Core.
    MemberName: MaxUnreliableQueuePerPeer
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Maximum unreliable packets queued per peer before the oldest are dropped.\n
      0 = scale automatically from population and available memory (recommended).\n\n
      This is the backstop that keeps an overloaded server alive. Unbounded, a server
      that\n cannot drain its send queue grows the backlog instead \u2014 measured
      at 2000 players, the\n queue reached ~40 GB before every peer timed out and
      the instance was lost. Bounded, the\n same overload costs dropped position
      updates and everyone stays connected.\n\n \u26A0\uFE0F It was a fixed 256,
      and that was too small to be only a backstop. At 2000 players the\n reduction
      system's per-tick fan-out exceeded it, so roughly half of every avatar\n update
      was destroyed here \u2014 and because dropping is far cheaper than sending,
      the\n producer saw fast ticks, concluded it had spare capacity, and increased
      its output.\n Raising it to 4096 on the same load measured zero drops, 22%
      more delivered bytes and\n 21% LESS CPU. Auto now sizes it per box; see `BasisPopulationScale`.\n\n
      Set a positive value only to pin it for a reproducible measurement."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
