    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Flipping one byte of each byte-field and every bit of each rotation
      field used to be the\n \"everything changed\" case, and used to force promotion
      because the old codec charged full\n width for any change at all. It no longer
      does: a one-byte flip of a 24-bit position axis is a\n bounded residual, so
      the delta stays genuinely smaller and shipping it is correct."
