  - TypeFullName: LiteNetLib.
    MemberName: SupportsBatchSend
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 1
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "True when SendBatch can hand the whole batch to the kernel in one call\n
      (Linux `sendmmsg`). Elsewhere the batch still works \u2014 it just costs one
      syscall per\n datagram, so only the managed-side per-send overhead is saved.\n
      Probed once at startup rather than assumed from the OS, because sendmmsg is
      absent on\n old kernels and blocked by some seccomp sandboxes."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
