  - TypeFullName: LiteNetLib.
    MemberName: MultiSocketCount
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Number of UDP sockets to bind on the same port using SO_REUSEPORT (Linux
      only).\n 1 (default) = single socket / single receive thread, current behavior.
      Values >1\n spawn additional sockets and receive threads so the Linux kernel
      RSS-hashes inbound\n datagrams across them, lifting the single-recv-thread
      pps ceiling. Each per-peer\n 4-tuple still hashes to one socket, so per-peer
      packet order is preserved.\n On non-Linux platforms this falls back to 1 with
      a warning logged at Start()."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
