  - TypeFullName: LiteNetLib.NetManager
    MemberName: PacketPoolSize
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Per-thread packet cache, in front of the shared pool.\n\n Every get
      and recycle used to touch the shared queue plus an interlocked counter, and
      at\n a few hundred thousand packets a second from every sending thread that
      contention was\n measurable: 7.9% of server CPU at 2000 players sat in PoolRecycle
      alone. A thread that\n recycles a packet is very likely to want one immediately
      afterwards, so almost all of\n that traffic can be served without leaving the
      thread.\n\n Static rather than per-manager on purpose. A NetPacket is a plain
      buffer with no\n affinity to whichever manager pooled it, and the load tester
      runs thousands of managers\n across a few dozen threads \u2014 one hot cache
      per thread beats one cold queue per manager.\n The shared pool stays as the
      balancing layer, which is what makes the asymmetry work:\n packets are often
      rented on a receive thread and recycled on a send thread, so a purely\n thread-local
      scheme would drain one side and overflow the other.\n\n Uses NetPacket.Next,
      which is already the pool's link field, so the list\n itself costs no allocation."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
