    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Whether opening a batch is worth it. Batching buys one syscall per
      batch instead of one\n per datagram \u2014 but only where the kernel can actually
      take a vector of datagrams.\n Without that the batch is a pure loss: every
      datagram pays an extra arena copy and the\n syscall count is unchanged. Measured
      at 500 players on Windows, batching cost +1.3\n cores for nothing, so there
      it stays off and the direct path is used unchanged."
