  - TypeFullName: LiteNetLib.SendBatcher
    MemberName: SendBatcher
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: IDisposable
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Collects outbound datagrams for one worker thread and hands them to
      the kernel together.\n\n A broadcast server's send cost is dominated by syscall
      count, not bytes: at 500 players the\n send loop issues ~165K datagrams/s,
      and the per-call transition costs more than building\n the packet did. Copying
      each datagram into an arena and flushing the arena with one\n `sendmmsg` trades
      a ~700-byte memcpy for a syscall, which is a large win on Linux and\n a small
      one elsewhere (the loop still costs one call per datagram, but pinning, exception\n
      frames and endpoint dispatch are paid once per batch).\n\n One instance per
      worker thread, so no synchronisation. Memory is unmanaged: the pointers\n handed
      to the kernel must stay put, and pinning a GC array for the lifetime of the
      server\n would fragment the heap it lives on."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
