    Summary: "Returns everything this peer still has queued to the packet pool. Called
      once when the\n peer is removed from the manager; without it every disconnect
      dropped up to a full\n unreliable queue plus any partial reassembly sets on
      the GC floor, and the shared pool\n replaced them with fresh allocations. Reliable-channel
      internals are deliberately left\n to the GC: their packets can still be referenced
      by an in-flight ack pass."
