  - TypeFullName: LiteNetLib.NetStatistics
    MemberName: NetStatistics
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Wire counters. Every field used to be a single `Interlocked` target,
      which meant one\n cache line ping-ponging between every core that sent a packet
      \u2014 at 500 players the send\n loop drives ~160K sends/s from ~30 threads,
      so the counters cost far more than the thing\n they were counting.\n\n Counters
      are striped across cache lines and each thread sticks to one stripe. The\n
      interlocked op stays (two threads can still hash to the same stripe, and a
      lost update\n would silently corrupt the totals the health endpoint reports)
      but it is now almost always\n uncontended, which is the part that was expensive."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
