  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.
    MemberName: IsTalking
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 2
    ParamNames:
    - index
    - '!_participates[index]'
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Speech is bursty: a person says something for a few seconds, then listens.
      Modelling it\n as a fixed always-on subset gets the average bitrate roughly
      right but none of the\n shape \u2014 no silence gaps, no changing set of speakers,
      and every recipient list exercised\n continuously rather than intermittently.
      Each participant alternates burst/silence with\n randomised durations, so who
      is talking keeps changing and most are quiet at any moment."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
