  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.Core.Compression.BasisAvatarDeadband
    MemberName: BasisAvatarDeadband
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Sub-quantization deadband for the local avatar uplink. Byte-identical
      suppression\n (BasisAvatarIdleSuppression) almost never fires in VR because
      sensor noise\n crosses quantization steps every frame; these primitives let
      the sender compare RAW\n (pre-quantization) values against the values of the
      last frame actually sent and drop the\n frame when every field moved less than
      a visibility threshold.\n\n Comparing against the last SENT frame (not the
      previous frame) bounds the standing error to\n the threshold itself: slow drift
      accumulates until it exceeds the deadband and then sends.\n Thresholds are
      chosen at or below the wire's own High-quality quantization step, so a\n suppressed
      change could barely have been expressed on the wire in the first place \u2014
      and the\n noise this suppresses is exactly the shimmer receivers otherwise
      have to low-pass away.\n\n Pure C# so BasisServerTests can cover it; quaternion
      dots run in double because the\n tightest thresholds (cos of hundredths of
      a degree) sit inside float epsilon of 1.0."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
