  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.Core.Compression.BasisAvatarDeltaCompression
    MemberName: BasisAvatarDeltaCompression
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Avatar delta compression against a keyframe baseline. A keyframe is
      the full fixed-size payload\n (BasisBoneRotationCompression.ConvertToSize).
      A delta encodes only the fields that\n changed since the last keyframe, preceded
      by a per-field dirty mask. Reconstructing a full\n payload = copy the baseline
      keyframe, then rewrite the dirty fields. Pure C#; shared by the\n server (encode)
      and client (decode), and used on the uplink in both directions.\n\n Fields:
      [0]=position, [1..31]=the rotation region's 31 wire fields (21 explicit bone
      rotations\n then 10 finger curl/splay channels), then scale, body rotation,
      hips delta, hips rotation and\n the end-effector block.\n\n \n\nDeltas reference
      the keyframe, never the previous frame. That is the property the\n whole fan-out
      depends on: the reduction system throttles each receiver to its own distance-derived\n
      send rate, so one sender's frames reach different receivers on different subsampling
      schedules.\n A single delta must therefore reconstruct the full pose on its
      own, regardless of which\n intermediate frames a given receiver was never sent
      or lost.\n\n\n\nBody encoding \u2014 per-channel residuals. Each dirty field
      is decomposed into its\n channels (BasisAvatarChannelMap) and each quantized
      channel is sent as the\n zig-zag Exponential-Golomb code of its difference
      from the baseline. Unchanged channels cost one\n bit, small motion three to
      seven. This is what buys per-component granularity: previously a bone\n whose
      single dominant axis moved by one quantization step cost its entire 38-bit
      field, and\n hinge joints \u2014 elbows, knees, every finger \u2014 move on
      one axis nearly all the time.\n\n\n\nResiduals are EXACT here, never companded.
      There is no closed loop against a keyframe\n baseline to absorb approximation
      error, so the reconstruction is bit-identical to the sender's\n payload. Exponential-Golomb
      can exceed a narrow channel's raw width, so every field also carries\n a mode
      bit and the encoder picks whichever encoding is shorter \u2014 bounding a field
      at its own\n verbatim size plus one bit, and with it the whole delta.\n\n\n\n
      Delta body layout:\n   [dirtyMask : DirtyMaskBytes][bitstream, LSB-first]\n
      and within the bitstream, for each dirty field in field order:\n   [1 bit mode][raw:
      every channel verbatim | residual: Raw channels verbatim, Delta channels as
      se(v)]\n The body is byte-padded at the end. Unlike the fixed-width scheme
      this replaces, the body length\n is not derivable from the mask alone \u2014
      DeltaBodyLength parses to find it."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
