    Summary: "HIGH quality. Since v52 only 3-DOF slots read their BPC entry \u2014
      restricted\n slots (BONE_DOF < 3) use the angle-bit tables instead. Bone slots
      0..20 = 606 bits;\n + 140-bit finger block = 746 bits = 94 rotation bytes.\n
      Per-finger priority: thumb/index get more bits (most expressive).\n Proximal
      gets more than intermediate/distal (carries spread motion)."
