    Summary: "Reduces a difference modulo 2^width into the signed range [-2^(width-1),
      2^(width-1)).\n Reconstruction masks back to the width, so this always round-trips
      exactly \u2014 and picking\n the short way round the ring keeps the code small
      when a signed field crosses zero."
