  - TypeFullName: Basis.Network.Server.Generic.BasisNetworkImageCache
    MemberName: BasisNetworkImageCache
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Keeps the bytes of every shared image in server RAM so a joining player
      can be handed the\n images already in the instance, instead of the original
      sharer having to send them all over\n again to each arrival.\n\n The cache
      is deliberately dumb about what an image *is*: it retains the client's own
      scene\n payloads verbatim and replays them stamped with the original owner's
      player id. A receiving\n client therefore sees exactly the OpSpawn/OpChunk
      stream it would have got from the owner,\n and needs no knowledge that the
      server answered instead.\n\n Lifetime matches what clients already do with
      images, so the cache can never show a joiner\n something the room cannot see:
      an entry is dropped on despawn and when its owner disconnects."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
