  - TypeFullName: BasisNetworkServer.BasisNetworkingReductionSystem.
    MemberName: intervalMs
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Current tick period in ms, adapted at runtime between MinTickIntervalMs
      and\n MaxTickIntervalMs.\n\n Ticking faster is NOT free and buys nothing below
      a point: clients publish at roughly 11 Hz\n and the shortest distance-derived
      send interval is 50 ms (20 Hz), so at the old fixed 250 Hz\n the loop spun
      12-20 times between any actual send to a given pair. Each of those ticks still\n
      paid full fork/join barriers on several Parallel loops, and split the work
      into batches too\n small to partition well. Slowing down under load therefore
      *increases* throughput: bigger\n batches, better parallel efficiency, fewer
      barriers \u2014 and no added latency while the period\n stays under the shortest
      send interval."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: BasisNetworkServer.BasisNetworkingReductionSystem.
    MemberName: MaxSpinMs
    Kind: Field
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "How many ticks the loop wants inside the shortest send interval, and
      so how far it is\n allowed to speed up when there is spare budget.\n\n The
      period only has to be fine enough to hit a pair's deadline without much jitter;\n
      beyond that, extra ticks find nothing due and pay fork/join on several Parallel
      loops for\n it. The old flat 4 ms floor meant a nearly idle server ran the
      whole tick machinery ~300\n times a second \u2014 measured at 500 players,
      scheduling was 59% of all server CPU, a flat\n ~1.1 cores that did not shrink
      with the population. Four ticks per interval bounds the\n added latency to
      a quarter of the shortest interval while running a third of the ticks."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
