  - TypeFullName: BasisNetworkServer.BasisNetworkingReductionSystem.ShardedConcurrentDictionary
    MemberName: ShardedConcurrentDictionary
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: System.Collections.Generic.IEnumerable<System.Collections.Generic.KeyValuePair<int,
      TValue>>
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Power-of-two-sharded ConcurrentDictionary<int, TValue> replacement.
      Splits writes\n across N=NextPow2(ProcessorCount) inner dicts indexed by a
      scrambled key, so per-bucket\n lock contention drops by ~N\xD7 under ingress
      storms (HandleAvatarMovement \u2192 currentMessages\n and ProcessMessage \u2192
      playerStates upserts at 1k+ players, 250Hz). Reference-swappable \u2014\n preserves
      the existing Interlocked.Exchange double-buffer pattern. Enumeration walks\n
      shards sequentially and inherits ConcurrentDictionary's per-shard snapshot
      semantics."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: BasisNetworkServer.BasisNetworkingReductionSystem.
    MemberName: DrainInto
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 1
    ParamNames:
    - shard
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Moves every value into `destination` and empties the dictionary.\n\n
      Deliberately not Clear: ConcurrentDictionary.Clear takes every bucket\n lock
      in the shard and rebuilds its table, so clearing all shards cost the same whether\n
      it held one message or a thousand. The tick loop drains ~19 messages several
      hundred\n times a second, and that fixed cost was the single most contended
      thing on the tick\n thread. Removing the keys we actually drained is proportional
      to the data instead, and\n only ever touches one bucket at a time.\n\n Anything
      written while this runs is simply picked up by the next drain, which is the\n
      same guarantee the previous swap-and-clear gave."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
