  - TypeFullName: BasisNetworkServer.BasisNetworkingReductionSystem.BSRThreadCounters
    MemberName: BSRThreadCounters
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "One worker thread's counter block. The send loop is a Parallel.For
      over receivers, so\n every counter below used to be an Interlocked op contended
      by every core at once \u2014\n bundleFallbacks alone ran ~130K/s at 500 players.
      Each thread now accumulates into its\n own block and BSRProfiler.TryPrint sums
      the registered blocks once per\n window, so the hot path is a plain non-atomic
      increment.\n\n Padded to keep two threads' blocks off the same cache line;
      without it the counters are\n contended by false sharing even though nothing
      is shared logically."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
