  - TypeFullName: Basis.Shims.BasisAvatarSwitchShim
    MemberName: BasisAvatarSwitchShim
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 1
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Bridges the persistent player's avatar-switch notification into the
      Cilbox\n sandbox. IBasisPlayer.OnAvatarSwitched is a true C# `event`\n (add_/remove_
      accessors), which sandboxed scripts cannot subscribe to. This\n native shim
      subscribes to it here (native code has no such restriction) and\n re-exposes
      it as the plain delegate PROPERTY Switched, which a\n sandboxed script can
      += / -=.\n\n It hangs off the PLAYER, not the avatar, so it survives avatar
      swaps \u2014 the\n avatar GameObject (and any shim on it) is destroyed and
      recreated on a switch,\n but the player, and this subscription, persist.\n\n
      No Cilbox whitelist entry is required: the type lives under Basis.Shims.* (already\n
      type-whitelisted), its members are ordinary property/Dispose calls, its constructor\n
      takes the already-whitelisted IBasisPlayer, and the only add_/remove_ on the
      true\n event happens in this native code \u2014 never in the sandbox."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
