  - TypeFullName: Basis.Shims.BasisBeforeRenderShim
    MemberName: BasisBeforeRenderShim
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: CilboxShim
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Gives a sandboxed script the late-latch callback that fires after all
      pose work for the frame\n but before anything is drawn \u2014 the place to
      pin something to the head, a hand or the camera\n without a frame of lag. `Update`/`LateUpdate`
      both run before Basis has finished\n solving IK, so a transform written there
      trails the head by a frame in VR.\n\n Declare `void OnBeforeRender()` and opt
      in once from `Start`:\n ```\n\n void Start() { GetComponent<BasisBeforeRenderShim>();
      }\n void OnBeforeRender() { transform.position = someHeadTransform.position;
      }\n \n```\n Cilbox creates the component on demand, so fetching it is the whole
      opt-in. The callback is\n resolved by name off the interpreted class and invoked
      directly \u2014 no host delegate is ever\n built for it, so there is no wrapper
      to leak and nothing to unsubscribe.\n\n This is the sandbox bridge onto BasisLocalCameraDriver.BeforeRender,
      which is\n the same hook native code uses. It runs with the whole render waiting
      on it, so keep the body\n short. It does not fire on a headless client, which
      never renders."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
