  - TypeFullName: Basis.Shims.BasisPlayersShim
    MemberName: BasisPlayersShim
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Roster access and pose reads for sandboxed scripts. Players ARE IBasisPlayer
      \u2014\n there is no parallel wrapper type. Identity comes straight off the
      interface\n (`player.DisplayName`, `player.PlayerPlatform`, `player.IsLocal`,
      \u2026); this\n class only supplies what the interface deliberately withholds.\n\n
      The withheld part is pose. Reading where someone is would otherwise mean handing
      over\n `AvatarTransform` or `BasisAvatar`, and a Transform is a write handle
      \u2014 a script\n could move, reparent or rescale another player. So the position
      and bone accessors here take\n a player and return a COPIED Vector3/Quaternion;
      the Transform never crosses the boundary.\n\n The per-player accessors are
      extension methods, so they read as members:\n ```\n\n foreach( IBasisPlayer
      p in BasisPlayersShim.All )\n     if( !p.IsConsideredFallBackAvatar )\n        
      Spawn( p.GetBonePosition( HumanBodyBones.Head ) );\n \n```"
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
