  - TypeFullName: Basis.Shims.BasisTransformSyncShim
    MemberName: GetValues
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 5
    ParamNames:
    - transforms
    - space
    - positions
    - rotations
    - '!doScale)'
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Read `transforms` into the arrays you pass. One invoke for the whole\n
      array instead of one per channel per transform.\n\n The arrays you pass ARE
      the channel selection: pass null for anything you do not want.\n `GetValues(bones,
      SpaceLocal, positions, rotations, null)` reads pose only and\n never touches
      scale.\n\n Entry i of each array corresponds to `transforms[i]`. The count
      processed is the\n shortest of the transform array and every non-null value
      array, capped at\n MaxPairs \u2014 nothing is ever read or written out of range.
      A destroyed or\n null transform is skipped and its slots are left as you had
      them, rather than being\n zeroed out from under you.\n\n Scale is always local:
      Unity's world scale (lossyScale) has no setter, so reading it\n would hand
      back something SetValues could not put back."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: "How many entries were considered \u2014 use it to bound your own loop."
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
  - TypeFullName: Basis.Shims.
    MemberName: SetValues
    Kind: Method
    ParamCount: 5
    ParamNames:
    - transforms
    - space
    - positions
    - rotations
    - '!doScale)'
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Write your arrays onto `transforms`. The exact mirror of\n GetValues,
      with the same rules: the arrays you pass are the channel\n selection, pairing
      is by index, the shortest length wins, and null or destroyed\n transforms are
      skipped.\n\n Round-tripping is lossless in local space \u2014 Get then Set
      with the same arrays and space\n leaves the hierarchy exactly as it was. In
      world space it is lossless for position and\n rotation but NOT for scale, because
      scale is always applied locally."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: How many entries were considered.
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
