  - TypeFullName: Basis.Shims.BasisVixxyShim
    MemberName: BasisVixxyShim
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Read-only metadata bridge for HVR Vixxy menu items. `HVRVixxyMenuItem`
      is whitelisted for avatar\n cilbox scripts pinned to GetValue/ApplyValue, which
      on its own is a bare float port \u2014 a script\n cannot tell a toggle from
      a slider, nor learn the valid range or the choice list.\n\n This exposes that
      metadata as primitives so `HVR.Vixxy.HVRVixxyControl` never has to be\n whitelisted:
      the control type stays host-side and only flattened values cross the sandbox\n
      boundary. Everything here is a read; writes still go through HVRVixxyMenuItem.ApplyValue.\n\n
      Vixxy menu items are wearer-only by design \u2014 on a remote avatar the control
      is never resolved and\n the value is meaningless. Scripts should gate on BasisAvatarShim.IsOwnedLocally
      before using any\n of this; HasControl is the cheap readiness check."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
