    IsStatic: 0
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 1
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Splices `list`'s rendered body back over the range it was parsed from.\n\n
      \n\nThe list must have been read from the same file contents that are on disk
      now, and\n must have round-tripped when it was parsed. Both are re-checked
      here: the body currently\n occupying the parsed range has to match a render
      of the list's original entries,\n otherwise the file changed underneath us
      or the parser never understood it, and the write\n is refused."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
