  - TypeFullName: Basis.Shims.Editor.BasisCilboxScriptScanner
    MemberName: BasisCilboxScriptScanner
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    BaseTypeName: 
    Interfaces: []
    IsAbstract: 0
    IsSealed: 0
    IsStatic: 1
    IsPartial: 0
    IsMemberStatic: 0
    IsMemberReadOnly: 0
    IsMemberConst: 0
    IsMemberVirtual: 0
    IsMemberOverride: 0
    Summary: "Works out what a script actually touches by walking the IL of its compiled
      method bodies.\n\n \n\nReading the method bodies rather than the type's public
      surface is the whole point: the\n sandbox refuses calls, and a call only appears
      in the body. A signature-level pass would say\n a script is fine while every
      line inside it is blocked.\n\n\n\nUses nothing but System.Reflection \u2014
      `GetILAsByteArray` plus\n `Module.ResolveMember` \u2014 so there is no IL library
      to vendor. The opcode table is read\n off OpCodes rather than hand-written."
    Remarks: 
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
    ExceptionCrefs: []
    ExceptionDocs: []
    SeeCrefs: []
    SeeAlsoCrefs: []
    Since: 
    ObsoleteMsg: 
    Platforms: []
